  <Content>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Center" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="General" id="4d35be5a-0353-4b54-826d-b8fcf202b379">
      <Text Style="Bold">“WALK THIS WAY”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="New Act" id="b21da113-011e-4dbd-9fb7-2eb0ea7e9ce8">
      <Text>ACT I:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Shot" id="9c53b396-d294-42a5-8602-b560b6c2dbec">
      <Text>FADE IN:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="6d2d4241-07cf-4557-a46b-4428ae48a96d">
      <Text>Rock music plays. A blend of the top hits and bands of the 70’s.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="d6728869-455f-469a-b2d5-dfa9d8c5968f">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="2" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. SUDBURY, MASSACHUSETTS, STREET - DAY (1979)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="14c8ae33-d6cc-4333-bcf9-ea5ca1977dd7">
      <Text>The sounds of suburban Boston drift through the air - kids playing street hockey, garage doors rumbling open, distant music from various houses creating a natural symphony.  A dog barks. A lawn mower starts up. Somewhere, a guitar amp crackles to life.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="2bdad062-39dc-4e06-88fe-44d790fb9a8e">
      <Text>FADE OUT.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Shot" id="469e347e-3964-4adf-8330-61c2d9bce11f">
      <Text>FLASHBACK - 1974</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Shot" id="7506482c-09d1-4b1b-ba9c-35c00e88e38e">
      <Text>SUPER: “FIVE YEARS AGO”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="5873f67a-3822-4713-98a6-2c2a752204fc">
      <SceneProperties Length="2" Page="2" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. EPHRAIM CURTIS MIDDLE SCHOOL, SUDBURY, MA - CAFETERIA - DAY </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="64bc6d2c-8658-413e-87ca-38e132cd89aa">
      <Text>The middle school cafeteria buzzes with typical colloquial chaos.  Brown bag lunches from mom, cafeteria on trays, jello, pizza, individual sized milk cartons ... kids mixing milk and jello like a science project.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="44d11233-6c47-4632-b854-d4dd7d85940a">
      <Text>DISCO MUSIC plays from someone’s radio - “Dancing Queen” fills the air. Most kids seem to accept it as normal background noise.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="d871b231-3dae-4542-99b8-3f159298f3d0">
      <Text>At a corner table, JACKIE MARSH (12) sits alone, clearly the new kid. He’s smaller than he’ll become but already carries himself with careful precision. He proudly wears a brown leather belt with a gold script “QUEEN” buckle as if it were an Olympic Gold Medal. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="acb4fd46-f6b3-4bab-82f5-52cc8bb8932b">
      <Text>NICK JOHNSON (12) enters the cafeteria, scanning for a place to sit. He’s wiry, already showing the restless energy that will define him. His black leather belt sports a chrome buckle with “AEROSMITH” in gothic letters.  </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="c2e78c68-a545-4390-8149-30e7531bbeae">
      <Text>The sun catches Nick’s buckle like a spotlight and for a brief instant the reflection blinds Jackie. As Nick walks closer their eyes meet. Not because they recognize each other, but because they both notice the other one’s belt buckle at the same time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="813373a3-be9b-4b96-a44e-8dedf4d77714">
      <Text>Nick walks over, confidence masking nervousness.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c4512101-ccec-41da-ad85-dea1d8509c9f">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f04b3258-0426-4776-848f-d172f1d076be">
      <Text>(pointing at Jackie’s buckle)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fea02f4b-f94f-4f92-b555-6088714058e8">
      <Text>Queen? Seriously?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="30811ae8-cf31-4514-8c0c-ab3e09292189">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="3952430f-da81-46cb-a8a0-3232e957f524">
      <Text>(defensive but curious)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8a1d2abc-6334-4400-835f-0e4bb8e7f9d8">
      <Text>What’s wrong with Queen?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4c709f5b-52bf-4146-a965-9e29cffb3199">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="83f6621f-a105-4173-a870-d6dd56b7d2cb">
      <Text>(grinning, proud of his own buckle)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6530e34e-b930-4839-a4ae-8cc9e79a4798">
      <Text>Nothing. Just ... Aerosmith’s better.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="630d70d7-4f5e-40c6-8b97-a17dc4815d1a">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="28e19261-df6c-4ed9-b764-e6fa934b30d9">
      <Text>(standing, simmering)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0f40c509-5b9c-4d8a-8d32-e0f7aa46c9cc">
      <Text>Better? Have you heard “Bohemian Rhapsody”?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a8eda5f7-a8ba-499d-95c9-cb4bb5045e48">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="3585ad3b-a68c-48fe-b53a-535ad46de5d5">
      <Text>(matching his energy)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3fa69eb8-e3fb-4398-b649-101400691b22">
      <Text>Have you heard “Dream On”?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="096a9cb8-70c2-437d-9b7a-ced5e7e48401">
      <Text>They stare at each other for a moment. The disco music continues playing around them - “Le Freak” now blasting from a radio.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9b1e1ec8-158d-4ac1-b84e-c33b13c8e91d">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="193508d9-6362-43fe-86e9-cf859ace3ad1">
      <Text>(disgusted, gesturing toward the music)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c24adedf-d1cf-4ffd-b00f-637e68b76add">
      <Text>Can we agree that disco sucks?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7957bf83-5041-4648-904f-f22c4bba1db2">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="6a85293a-e0bb-4604-8258-85228ba7de15">
      <Text>(immediate bonding)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5fe3f36c-fcf3-47c5-a7b8-13b39d9fadf3">
      <Text>Oh my God, finally someone who gets it! It’s like ... music without soul.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="488b135e-bf7f-41fd-8ac5-e9e9f30aeeba">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="a7b3a9ab-4ea5-434f-b524-3b789792f9d3">
      <Text>(excited)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="570bf4cd-bb5a-4e9a-9f55-34801c9f23ab">
      <Text>Exactly! Where’s the artistry? Where’s the emotion?  What is a “Bee Gee” anyway?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c1139d5a-5428-4548-bba1-35aa3944ac7a">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="13e1d2dd-4236-4e75-92f0-1b9f16b7f927">
      <Text>(sitting down)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e567d95f-c6bc-417b-8503-763b9a592733">
      <Text>I’m Nick. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="be9fd05e-397a-4f49-ab3c-5f53a0d8867d">
      <Text>(extending his hand)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="512390dc-e96e-4491-b2c2-8e441bc94853">
      <Text>I think I saw you earlier in Mr. Apfel’s homeroom. I just didn’t see that buckle of yours.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="59ab6a3d-0c40-4145-abd3-3130ed16fa9f">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="74bd6b5c-1480-4dbf-8263-a6331d05c4e6">
      <Text>Jackie. My dad just moved us here from Ithaca.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4476c54b-fcdf-416b-b407-c110f2b0fb53">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="abf97ea5-61e2-4503-9cf6-fc22069da911">
      <Text>(leaning forward)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1e79916b-74f6-497b-bc5c-f77e3803ca98">
      <Text>So ... Queen versus Aerosmith. This is happening?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="74587bc8-ea70-485e-b607-5473e5189199">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="0d8c6559-c4dc-4f51-897e-74638ce731cf">
      <Text>(grinning)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d803632b-b21c-4146-a225-cf112acb81ba">
      <Text>Oh, it’s happening.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="4eb05aba-342b-447e-be71-28e893b8cefd">
      <Text>The Bee Gees “Staying Alive” can be heard in the background with several middle schoolers now cooly singing the chorus while rocking their heads back and forth to the disco beat.  Jackie and Nick just shake their heads in disgust.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="2b00016d-11ec-4afd-83f7-b2489ea83713">
      <Text>CUT TO:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="92ddb5fd-ecbe-4135-9535-d8c65f718d14">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 5/8" Page="4" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BOTH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. JOHNSON FAMILY GARAGE - DAY (SAME 1974 FLASHBACK)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="4eb05aba-342b-447e-be71-28e893b8cefd">
      <Text>The garage is cluttered but welcoming. Nick and Jackie sit on milk crates, guitars in hand. The “versus” debate has evolved into the beginning of musical collaboration. Some basic Aerosmith and Queen paraphernalia scattered about.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4ea97e3b-517f-4b7d-8c92-dd7da3e73e39">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="7a7d399e-8b32-470f-b31d-e2862b2a6d96">
      <Text>(strumming)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="819422eb-8a01-4c39-a63a-115627aee94a">
      <Text>Okay, but listen to this ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="5f1d756b-c7aa-4327-a89f-9d9576e1bf3a">
      <Text>He plays the opening to “Sweet Emotion.” The garage seems to pulse with the rhythm.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="38b191de-01f6-496c-b6a6-2eb5e276c804">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="469d3f3c-2d36-49e4-9e04-d55399ab95b1">
      <Text>(impressed)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="427d4733-b674-4e9d-86a7-5c25c8dff4a0">
      <Text>That’s half-decent. Check out what I’ve been working on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="747f5a4d-64fc-404b-8923-a1dfc08550db">
      <Text>Jackie plays the piano part to “Bohemian Rhapsody” on his guitar. The garage acoustics create an almost cathedral-like effect.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="821781f2-459f-4c06-9ed2-9973c4392f27">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="5912d735-5e73-4b28-bf66-19ccfde9db9b">
      <Text>(awed)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d7ba31a9-a9ee-4015-80ef-ce3844efbceb">
      <Text>Holy shit, Jackie. That’s like ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="36a55d0a-8a6d-4886-a44c-e67c6c0905ce">
      <Text>(thinking)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="400a9558-86de-4880-bd19-55f0b01895a0">
      <Text>That’s like fucking operatic.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8772953c-5c35-45b4-b38f-637911aeccdf">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="7d2cfc9e-e8d8-4530-ae88-2550997f4296">
      <Text>(fatherly, but joking)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ffb62051-6cb9-4caf-a4fc-e72e3f078184">
      <Text>Language, Nicholas. But thank you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bd1c951a-4c77-4fb4-ad08-e7a42d631b8f">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ec35a840-4c95-42ab-a90e-8ea8802b958a">
      <Text>(suddenly serious)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c1e0e32b-03ea-4403-8096-a2a9cdd2ab03">
      <Text>You know what? We should start a band.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0762fe70-18ed-4710-9abd-dd2a7e6a6c0c">
      <Text>Jackie</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f035a432-a09a-416f-a3a9-f962f044d618">
      <Text>(laughing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0d0a0653-35ff-41cd-9bc8-9155127be559">
      <Text>What would we call it? “Queen Smith”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5eaff2b6-2029-4942-8936-d7f9632fe46e">
      <Text>Nick</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="2d40e8ad-ba55-4d3d-9e24-d4494e79b916">
      <Text>(deadpan)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d516965e-62c6-47e8-8cb0-34a49d1ec502">
      <Text>“Aero Queen”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="58958c0c-83a9-4add-8182-56a1991aa964">
      <Text>The both burst into laughter. The sound echoes in the garage, creating natural harmonies. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f04f4e62-2b4e-417b-b5b4-94dfa3b6b815">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3c929414-a4f5-4beb-a3a8-8287fe7cc928">
      <Text>What if we did both? Like ... what if we took the best of both worlds?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fcc264b7-e892-4cf7-827e-b624a55a32d4">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1c77af9b-5011-493a-a70e-61ba143cc1b8">
      <Text>Raw power meets technical precision?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="66e5118e-4354-404e-954c-eb1ed41a73d2">
      <Text>They begin to play together. Nick’s “Sweet Emotion” riff under Jackie’s “Bohemian Rhapsody” melody. It shouldn’t work, but it does. The garage fills with magical sound. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="04b4cb65-3055-47d7-ba86-684d180067ff">
      <Text>BOTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="380636cf-77d8-443e-bd2b-ea3d797a5eab">
      <Text>(singing together, voices blending)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="57733af6-9b1f-4ad2-bf47-3b51a8419740">
      <Text>Sweet Emotion ... Is this the real life ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Note" id="f1a0e2f8-45b0-4196-b337-909babcc5a14">
      <Text>*** Musical Moment</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="f5145bb5-c19c-487b-bb2a-a6dae3b3b14c">
      <Text>The music become environmental - tools vibrate, sunlight pulses, the very air seems to dance with the harmony.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ef2b445c-9976-4429-a2e1-dff758ef6883">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="18bcbf66-f819-439e-8131-dfbe67ce7c33">
      <Text>(stopping, breathless)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="02e0323f-ff8a-49e8-beb2-7eaab098505d">
      <Text>We could do this.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b959ce06-2f37-4d0b-9159-8e4f575b6365">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="a21bc28b-49d0-4c80-b56b-512b627ef1de">
      <Text>(equally excited)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b81c22f6-19de-452f-a4f4-3d8e0d0b55c3">
      <Text>We could change everything.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="d5ffcfc2-96e6-4875-9fd2-0cf46243d2fb">
      <Text>CUT TO:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="6ef96daa-8b1b-4f85-b9da-e0c6ce4645f9">
      <SceneProperties Length="1/8" Page="6" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. SAME garage - day - (present 1979)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="a30bbb75-7868-4beb-8769-33bff8fd2c71">
      <Text>The same garage but transformed. The garage is now clearly dedicated solely to Aerosmith with lots of posters, scarves, stickers, faded concert T-shirts and the controlled chaos of someone channeling Steven Tyler ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="0dfba009-1f6f-44b8-8f6e-cd2df146cad3">
      <SceneProperties Length="1/8" Page="6" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>TITLE CARD:  “WALK THIS WAY”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="1d181f99-6ddc-4c98-a3e2-2ee280d27048">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 5/8" Page="6" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DR. MARSH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MRS. MARSH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. Marsh family kitchen - mORNING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="4ad6b561-3775-4daa-b5ab-d1f598d9d463">
      <Text>The breakfast table is set with formal precision. JACKIE MARSH (17) now tall and lean with natural stage presence, sits “trapped” across from his parents.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="2ec99c1c-cef1-42c9-8954-84cc4576eb5b">
      <Text>DR. RICHARD MARSH (45) reads the business section of the Boston Globe while eating his traditional breakfast. His callused fingers suggest he once played guitar himself - a detail Jackie doesn’t know. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="2ec99c1c-cef1-42c9-8954-84cc4576eb5b">
      <Text>Dr Marsh moved the family to Sudbury for a better suburban life as he switched jobs from economics professor at Ithaca College to Director of Economics at Boston University.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="9fd13026-fb35-43c9-9cae-ab091284f53e">
      <Text>MRS. HELEN MARSH (42) pours coffee for Dr. Marsh with the efficiency of someone who’s given up her own dreams for family stability.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7cabaa2c-2952-49ce-a181-2bd65563270b">
      <Text>DR. Marsh</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="23686337-7a84-4aae-bd83-94232209e493">
      <Text>(not looking up from the paper)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aa1a3691-fd27-4a87-91ae-67ef50066bff">
      <Text>I saw the letter from Cornell.  Any thoughts ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c67c28c4-aa1f-4797-9371-f7326d7c214f">
      <Text>MRS. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="697e4c07-df8a-44d1-a394-591056bdb1f1">
      <Text>... and Berkeley called yesterday. They are interested in your classical training and your plans for next year.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fcabc633-7059-4554-9a4c-2a718b07302d">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="6938fc79-7597-4d97-a052-607fa59e0245">
      <Text>(half ignoring)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f2b25fdd-206f-40ab-9e78-86447e80a534">
      <Text>I’ve been thinking thinking about my OWN band.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="5e85f49f-2eb3-4a34-ba29-c233cf297151">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="88aaa690-a8b1-4595-8f40-c8cb19cd28dd">
      <Text>While I still keep up with my training and my 4.0.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5d4acb6a-ca0e-4f69-beca-f7f48012611e">
      <Text>MRS. Marsh</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="8e9ab597-2ff3-46db-ae20-9bc7e927ad11">
      <Text>(sitting dow, gentle but firm)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="203f8cf8-78cb-40a5-bad2-606eb00f5776">
      <Text>Darling, you have a gift. A real gift ... but the “Freddie Mercury’s” of the world are one in a million.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c6be6eb9-ad41-4ebb-9b46-7bfa871c03e5">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="de0655ec-b938-4a9c-a91a-3806fdc7c838">
      <Text>(passionate)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0e0ca34b-2c2c-459b-a2ce-310e7ce0cf55">
      <Text>But that’s exactly why I need to try!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f9a51abd-f95b-44d6-aa30-10f53f1cb453">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0e0ca34b-2c2c-459b-a2ce-310e7ce0cf55">
      <Text>Freddie paved the way, the way he brings opera to rock, the way he makes music theatrical ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0e9d85c9-4abf-42d4-b3df-e21abb880c2a">
      <Text>DR. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="85036edb-a8a2-40b5-88eb-0d0b0c7a20cd">
      <Text>(finally looking up, pain in his eyes)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="df2505e7-1651-4c0a-b16b-928a902f837c">
      <Text>I know the dream. I do. But dreams don’t pay the bills. Business school does.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="559c58b5-8a27-4f3d-98db-3811dd348b85">
      <Text>There’s as story in his father’s voice - regret, perhaps his own abandoned musical aspirations.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="22a7268e-d398-443c-9f87-d3360537d715">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="c4f10967-df6e-4db6-9c94-1ab714515efc">
      <Text>(noticing his father’s expression)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="23687b30-92ff-465c-a834-1a609f0ceb54">
      <Text>Dad ... did you ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d54cd0e4-549b-4a50-b186-51e7fcdc0453">
      <Text>DR. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="63cabea5-a561-4f0f-95f5-5db3a3c4da20">
      <Text>(quickly returning to his paper)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="74ad9e2b-b67c-4de1-838e-a07a195ca40a">
      <Text>I don’t want you to make the same mistakes ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="f004edd6-e97f-4c61-aad2-5ec471dd05e1">
      <Text>From upstairs, a violin interrupts this “Jackie’s future” moment. The sound plays - beautiful, precise, classical. The melody drifts down from above like silk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="7ec58048-326f-487b-84f6-fe6235500d4a">
      <Text>ELIZABETH MARSH (13) is a prodigy, Jackie’s younger sister and a freshman at the Lincoln-Sudbury Regional High School. She has short brown hair and freckles resembling Scout from the movie, “To Kill A Mockingbird”.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bda5eab2-09ef-4dfb-b917-9f2435c6003f">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="3d603b8f-440d-4b47-89f5-fbffd1f07a1f">
      <Text>(smiling)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f1e47876-8869-4d69-a230-4dff05a2baee">
      <Text>Elizabeth practices twice as hard as anyone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cbd73226-230c-403f-9526-e6a2a12c79c4">
      <Text>MRS. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="3ba178fc-276f-42ed-93c7-3266bad0870f">
      <Text>(proudly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="28221f08-c453-42fc-8567-2c40933bef2b">
      <Text>She’s been accepted to the regional symphony. Only thirteen and already principal violin.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9e560ff9-7f31-4676-a9da-25f697007f4d">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="be1d0b39-7ba0-4da8-8038-1a88f82a07a2">
      <Text>(and idea forming)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fa04a297-21a2-4af7-b178-ab0b041476c9">
      <Text>What if ... our classical training could help with rock music?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2f9a46ab-f909-48db-abda-5bb91f728321">
      <Text>DR. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f77cd164-92d6-41aa-a726-213997cc9bbf">
      <Text>(skeptical, but glancing over his newspaper)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d55fc29f-0b02-4681-b06a-c9b3fa8f282e">
      <Text>How do you mean?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="982daf8f-aefb-4296-967a-aadae862a161">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f6035498-cbb3-4f66-890e-7127bc8e1a9a">
      <Text>(excited)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="681873d3-3383-4543-b829-d87a34c56411">
      <Text>Freddie Mercury had operative training. That’s what makes Queen so unique. They bring artistry to rock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="c1e8df90-7453-4731-8ba5-dbd8481ffade">
      <Text>Almost on cure the violin upstairs shifts into a rock-influenced melody - Elizabeth experimenting with her classical training. We hear Queen’s “Can’t Stop Me Now” modeling her other brother’s obsession.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="034e4132-be48-4634-a296-9294da2c78c9">
      <Text>MRS. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="2d8b07f8-7130-4051-b4f7-1229489a6f3b">
      <Text>(listening to the violin)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="da9ebce2-dfa7-42f2-879b-ec6fed846428">
      <Text>She’s quite talented, isn’t she?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7d177069-f3f7-46f4-94da-34ae9d6fc872">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="21807da1-75a5-4222-abc1-0ab93dfe64ba">
      <Text>(grinning)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="49badba1-b9d5-48cd-be04-97108d24bd99">
      <Text>She’s incredible. And she’s been encouraging me about the band.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4506bdf1-c935-460e-9526-034e50d1c5ac">
      <Text>DR. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="8e508d2c-cf77-4643-af2e-ecd1e89befc9">
      <Text>(warning)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4ec22782-ddd9-45d0-87b1-cc3b1f9f7b97">
      <Text>Jackie, don’t drag your sister into all of this ... this ... this nonsense.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e573bc67-99a9-46a6-bf42-7ee042b24215">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="7964e028-24af-4884-9f59-dc861b695213">
      <Text>(standing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="01bf3c78-12e8-44ce-8e34-f4f03b5d5036">
      <Text>It’s not nonsense, Dad. It’s art. It’s rock and roll ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="73a31f3e-d6cc-4dd9-9719-aee751ba40d5">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="8" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MARY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. Johnson family house - same morning</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="e5e6b345-709c-4753-93e0-ff0d35265fce">
      <Text>A modest two-story home. The lawn needs cutting. A rusty pickup sits in the driveway. A Honda motorcycle has seen better days.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="10684ce9-8059-404d-8778-34e0fd67a584">
      <Text>NICK JOHNSON (17) now embodies Steven Tyler’s raw energy and attitude. He moves with restless energy while eating Captain Crunch cereal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b4e9c622-b4e6-4a6f-b815-a17784bc96a4">
      <Text>MARY JOHNSON (38) rushes around in her Friendly’s uniform (diner). Her movements are efficient, born from years of working multiple jobs, but there’s a dignity in her struggle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bc4b116b-4cd7-4c74-9f1e-4e789e4a5d72">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="6be83d6d-a507-4a28-8df8-ceb2ecf9d16e">
      <Text>(grabbing car keys)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c43888d3-8ccf-4f39-b287-ad978293f1e4">
      <Text>I’m pulling a double at Friendly’s then helping Deb clean merchandise that new store, Duck Soup.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="30a38776-8cc1-4696-aeee-0d9c015edb5b">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1d4357e4-bf76-4296-a40d-939d7fc09bca">
      <Text>There’s meatloaf in the fridge.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="295991e2-7f3b-4640-b44e-cf1f7a422021">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="225dba2b-b9da-4ce7-a1f8-27ceaeb13503">
      <Text>(passionately optimistic)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="89136235-1f8b-4eda-a0f9-3ee3e5336d27">
      <Text>Mom, when I make it you’ll never have to work this hard again. I’m going to finally form my </Text>
      <Text Style="Bold+Italic">own</Text>
      <Text> band. I’m ready.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="15ae02b1-5d4f-41f1-bd0a-639359b069f2">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="d5b722b3-c5c7-443f-ad59-c34a9b0704ef">
      <Text>(stopping)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="843ea95f-09f7-4ab8-8538-d7d05e608afe">
      <Text>Baby, I work hard because I love you. Not because I must.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="81566e1d-b684-44d2-9e49-5ffae2c4d13a">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="5d7cc62d-2059-4da4-902c-ccc02277c5e2">
      <Text>(vulnerable)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aabb3355-4b4a-48fd-a9b4-974194890cad">
      <Text>But don’t you want more?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ca40745e-c62b-4add-afdb-715cb754a707">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="408eaa4a-20f0-4cb4-97a8-c9cb2ef976a0">
      <Text>(sitting down momentarily)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="76f6c036-b848-4320-b86b-96244405a8d3">
      <Text>I want you, mister, to be happy. Really happy. Not just successful happy.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="de317253-f09c-41e9-815a-d684c8e49c94">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="c7fbdb3a-99a9-4cab-86a2-70c77cface27">
      <Text>(confused)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="92fc0d4c-2951-4303-891c-5fc6a63f4f19">
      <Text>What’s the difference?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d27391e0-124d-4cfe-8007-0ff1ebbcaceb">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="8840faf1-bfc6-499b-936f-409072607116">
      <Text>(wise)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="adc85f0b-abf2-41fb-adb6-af29f707ac90">
      <Text>Success is not beating other people.  Happiness is about being true to yourself.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="324fe57c-3640-463e-8af7-ff7712c42ef7">
      <Text>She head for the door, then turns back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="36ff5d5f-834f-4a0b-9bd1-33d35094d402">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dc9fa8df-260a-4595-a1ad-37342a82da51">
      <Text>You talk to Jackie?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7f1ebe11-f5ab-4377-bebd-b93f82780198">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="a8165c68-49e1-4e4f-a451-0658922ea9cd">
      <Text>(defensive)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="62a5bf30-4f3b-46ac-b0b3-cb186864898e">
      <Text>Why would I talk to someone who things he’s better than me, better than us?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4843f7d0-4835-47ba-afb2-84f8d9791e54">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="89f88b11-26bf-4449-adb6-ffd8d2344029">
      <Text>(gently)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="815be247-17d2-4524-9b7e-f9ad50bb0e81">
      <Text>Maybe he’s hurting too.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="6e9e79ac-114a-4720-8278-26a3e6b1ee24">
      <Text>She leaves. Nick stares at the empty doorway, the truth hitting home.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="5a5193cf-7673-4f72-ad6d-fd6d61a679c9">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="10" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. Lincoln-sudbury regional high school, sudbury - daY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="8e8531be-fc2b-4d57-8d1f-27ff4c218a6b">
      <Text>Students stream in, social hierarchies visible in their clothing and car choices. The music playing from various cars and boom boxes creates a cacophony of competing sounds.  A musical transition as Rock takes over Disco.  Somehow the music and movement work together as synchronized high school chaos.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="0b97842f-c0c2-4b48-8159-20400d4a7167">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 4/8" Page="10" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. LINCOLN-SUDBURY HIGH SCHOOL cafeteria - day</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="40b44f3d-e6ee-4be0-a44c-7cfdb75ba461">
      <Text>The cafeteria is divided by invisible social lines.  Jackie sits with the college-bound crowed - polo shirts, khakis, discussing SAT scores, Ivy League early acceptance letter and what the future holds. They sit in an elevated potion of the of the cafeteria known as the “The Ramp” where all the cool kids sit.  They are not so affectionately known as the “</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RAMPERS</Text>
      <Text>”.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="cc4ff86c-bfe3-4533-81b6-20fbfc56b6fa">
      <Text>Nick sits with the working-class kids and it’s a melting pot of backgrounds from the greasers (known as “RATS”) and the regular kids (”REGS”) the ones who just try to fit in. Their wardrobes consists mostly of white T-shirts and faded jeans. They discuss jobs, weekend beer parties and gossip about which of the RATS were caught smoking pot in infamous L-S High School “Glass Corridor”.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="53945126-fd8c-4850-8d75-e0bda7c6cde9">
      <Text>From atop The Ramp someone’s boom box plays Queen’s “We are the Champions”. It’s a catchy tune and the volume is turned up. Jackie can’t help himself - he begins conducting the invisible orchestra, his classical training evident in his precise movements.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2b492b45-530c-45df-91d7-2b730a34e275">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="35910724-d4e4-4606-b264-3f6bce2a2fe6">
      <Text>(singing under his breath)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="76e9caad-72ba-462c-8fbc-6fbd2a2a053c">
      <Text>We are the champions, my friends...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Note" id="65101ddd-2c7e-44fd-9a87-8c69a32112de">
      <Text>*** Musical Moment</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="255937d7-13b9-4fcf-accd-460300dc4366">
      <Text>Suddenly Jackie’s table joins in perfect rhythm with the STOMP, STOMP, CLAP ... STOMP, STOMP, CLAP ... and soon all of The Ramp members join in. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="03f2894f-51f9-4975-88c2-81ab3ad59a17">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="2a96f54d-6be5-41e1-ac7d-a0bb21de01c5">
      <Text>(singing growing louder and louder)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8dbd5a70-a947-4b06-b0e4-4bd23752aa1d">
      <Text>I’ve paid my dues</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8dbd5a70-a947-4b06-b0e4-4bd23752aa1d">
      <Text>time after time </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8dbd5a70-a947-4b06-b0e4-4bd23752aa1d">
      <Text>I’ve done my sentence</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8dbd5a70-a947-4b06-b0e4-4bd23752aa1d">
      <Text>But committed no crime ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="e055d740-0643-4692-9a96-75cf89035350">
      <Text>Across the cafeteria , Nick hears the building musical and grimaces. He grabs his friends boom box and cranks up Aerosmith’s “Walk This Way”. His body starts to move with Stephen Tyler’s distinctive swagger as if Nick has been waiting for this moment his whole life. He grabs another kid’s banana to use as his mic.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="604e1381-193f-4eea-a486-e18b496803b9">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="a0b333c2-02d9-4dd9-a506-51f5ecc79eba">
      <Text>(singing with raw power)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="03480d28-fc07-4340-a6e2-7020ffe4c9c9">
      <Text>... Wasn’t me she was foolin’</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="03480d28-fc07-4340-a6e2-7020ffe4c9c9">
      <Text>‘Cause she knew what she was doin’ And I know love was here to stay When she told me to ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f15e1bed-76b5-4356-bb0a-e7c564cb18b2">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8a5e5115-4a91-44f7-9f73-eab10ba4bcb4">
      <Text>WALK THIS WAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7af914f6-cd1f-4d2c-aa73-7928a1628060">
      <Text>WALK THIS WAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e5cda3ed-fbf2-48ce-b575-f0ebbf836c9f">
      <Text>WALK THIS WAY ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="081e6bb3-af98-4979-a3b1-075d44cc21f5">
      <Text>Nick’s table bangs cafeteria utensils in rhythm - messier, more rebellious, more authentic. The cafeteria becomes a musical battleground. Back and forth. Two different approaches to rock and roll class in the same space. In the chaos, Jackie and Nick lock eyes for a split second. The challenge is is issued without words spoken aloud.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e1cfa48f-9559-402f-a295-5fcd1129ae85">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="8abacb62-eeb7-4688-b6c5-41cf9fedcf06">
      <Text>(to himself)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d589a71e-ad81-4e3d-8906-9fb546ca6a9c">
      <Text>It’s happening.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0c765af7-ddfa-4c55-b5bf-d66d2f9987cc">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="47af989b-150b-4f48-a5b9-33db93bedbdb">
      <Text>(to himself)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fe85f943-7fb7-4da7-97f6-289521efd3ac">
      <Text>Oh, it’s happening.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="ef4b66d1-4bd7-4e76-9d2a-4a039ba2ecba">
      <Text>Reminiscent of their first Queen-Aerosmith middle school encounter.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="ade32fe2-8108-452f-b77f-b5f946f0e677">
      <Text>CUT TO:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="48c5c756-17ce-4624-a596-cd426c98ee61">
      <SceneProperties Length="1/8" Page="11" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. LiNCOLN-SUDBURY REGIONAL HIGH SCHOOL - West hall - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="72c86d80-41fc-4f85-a7dc-b00402c3619b">
      <Text>The “REGS” gather around a black and white poster on the walls of the safe confines of West Hall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="5984c6eb-3d5a-4ad3-af70-18413eb20c63">
      <SceneProperties Length="1/8" Page="12" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. lincolN-SUDBURY HIGH - glass corridor - day</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="94d1638c-93a6-498b-835b-b2d842033b61">
      <Text>The “RATS” gather around a black and white poster newly taped within the not-so-safe confines of the Glass Corridor. Cigarette smoke permeates the Glass Corridor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="004b9909-7cf5-4276-b1c0-432413033a09">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="12" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MR. WENTWORTH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. LinCOLN-SUDBURY HIGH HIGH SCHOOL - music room - day</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b8142e2d-44ec-4523-be87-5d505336f9d1">
      <Text>L-S music teacher MR. BOB WENTWORTH (55) finishes pinning the same poster on one of the music room bulletin boards. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b8142e2d-44ec-4523-be87-5d505336f9d1">
      <Text>An accomplished musician in his own right, Mr. Wentworth wears his signature bow tie, salt &amp; pepper beard and long hair in a pony tail. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="595b71fe-15aa-4abb-9484-2876d78d173a">
      <Text>The bulletin boards are cluttered with upcoming school events, music instrument want ads, musical lesson advertisements.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="0d64ec5e-cec2-4f08-a753-7a77713d1663">
      <Text>Jackie and Nick enter from opposite doors drawn in for the same reason.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="947fb418-0dfb-44fa-990e-342e26fac94a">
      <Text>MR. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="08845c9f-fd96-4e7d-82cf-cc9c4fb19b65">
      <Text>Gentlemen, I see you’ve both must have seen the poster. We are switching up the spring musical and trying something new.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="626340fd-7fa8-4b54-bf6d-72ab3895d618">
      <Text>On the board the poster reads: </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="4ecec888-4265-45cf-a173-7cf303f34a68">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 4/8" Page="12" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MR. WENTWORTH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text Style="">“BATTLE OF THE BANDS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="fddd541c-0a44-4da6-8602-e6d01db59b6f">
      <Text>MARCH 15TH, 1979</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="90069b8b-c02f-4ca7-a725-5ab868c50b8e">
      <Text>EIGHT BANDS MAXIMUM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="d2ae8e2e-959d-409e-a590-e845714534ac">
      <Text>REGIONAL COMPETITION”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f043d82a-7dd7-4a83-bfc5-c06c89dadc33">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="b40c95d6-cd8a-465f-b7c1-08b621bf2e8f">
      <Text>(reading)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="23b6f266-94c9-4188-bdcf-dfc92c89107e">
      <Text>“Grand prize: $500 and professional recording session.”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="960a3d0b-c770-44ae-a5d2-07dcac8f2ffe">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="c948970e-ac99-4d45-ad11-926bb5abf65b">
      <Text>(reading)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1cc32837-2001-47c6-a1aa-a57f4d290197">
      <Text>“Judged by WBCN’s own “The Rock of Boston” Jerry “The Duke of Madness” Goodwin, Tami </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Heide</Text>
      <Text>, Carter Alan and </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Maxanne</Text>
      <Text> Satori.”  </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="942d59db-80e5-4c4f-857d-8c05621ed698">
      <Text>They lock eyes and tension is electric. Two best friends that have drifted apart.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9e018b3b-5847-46b9-a0dd-22499228a277">
      <Text>MR. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ef9a4706-2f77-4456-857d-1bc3a7c85afb">
      <Text>(hopefully)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="99304d4c-9931-4c0c-b532-5a13f8605916">
      <Text>You know, there’s nothing stopping you two from-</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="abda07bd-6d6e-4385-9c07-370c07b4ca8d">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="747268dd-762a-4145-b123-91b897069079">
      <Text>(interrupting)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b9333ca8-d21f-4f3e-9c6f-41f690098f85">
      <Text>We’ll be entering separately.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c49beab7-c668-4e94-bee7-d6edf7221e49">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="9a862b35-aa88-4249-9db8-612fce88969e">
      <Text>(simultaneously)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9564285b-0155-4ecc-9245-d33d5fb6bd4d">
      <Text>Damn right we will.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d053e259-930e-4777-a53b-c354348ede38">
      <Text>MR. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="a0a63fbb-cb25-4f3f-b28c-6a150241a514">
      <Text>(sighing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b5fa1754-c178-49a7-8748-3f1c872be589">
      <Text>I was afraid of that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="41741317-9a31-46c8-8e8c-117e97ae3d87">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="89e5691e-181a-400b-bc0d-186a830e010d">
      <Text>I never told you, but I attended the ‘75 Curtis Middle School Talent Show. Everyone thought Chris Bacon was going to win it all, but you two brought the house down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="c9058577-714e-433f-a15a-a1ddc4044999">
      <Text>(remembering)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ee3117dd-079a-42ce-bb23-951a424eeb87">
      <Text>Beautiful music.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="e32eeafc-4d26-427c-ae66-02add50247a1">
      <Text>*** This is critical dialogue that need to be consistent, but not repetitive ***</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8bae3452-3288-4206-9b3d-f5c7e94ac579">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="7b3b5dee-4867-4afb-8c3a-a44d5ab017cc">
      <Text>(accusatory)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1723c7da-5831-4664-9811-70ce4dff3cde">
      <Text>That was before Nick decided that Aerosmith was the only real rock music.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b025e6b1-79d5-4d4e-bd81-212122a1a1b7">
      <Text>Nick</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="cb6c0f78-c468-4fde-b56f-5847b9981534">
      <Text>(bitter)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7449fcf1-03bd-49a0-92b0-4574cb5bab28">
      <Text>That was before Jackie and Queen become too sophisticated for working-class kids.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3809d00d-18d8-4e0a-8624-265d9830ad06">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c455b2b0-b0ea-4cf3-9e75-b302ee5626f5">
      <Text>You shut me and the world out when ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="856169d4-7b66-438c-bff6-ce8410c80788">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="e587e9b0-1c5f-48b3-bdeb-25f2e17fedf2">
      <Text>(snapping)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dcc7de88-64f1-4f64-bc7e-32421446f2e4">
      <Text>When what? I needed you ... </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ac3a9906-9e7c-49a1-947a-e7f7b6b3633b">
      <Text>Mr. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="1bd2367e-6d20-40ff-bc0c-6693f8fcb40a">
      <Text>(stepping in between)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0fd07709-930d-46dc-a6f0-55bc33e73e9b">
      <Text>Boys, you’re both wrong. Music is about class or sophistication or who’s better. It’s about truth and bringing people together.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="271bf984-1d34-473d-984f-45afc84fdb08">
      <Text>Nick and Jackie stare at each other, the weight of their broken friendship heavy in the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="d75a9cf5-1636-4491-91ee-6981f43b4951">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 2/8" Page="14" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ELIZABETH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. MARSH FAMILY house - living room - night</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="34e2ad02-87c0-4303-bc5f-8ac142b01a11">
      <Text>Jackie sits at the piano, working out arrangements. Elizabeth enters with her violin as if it were another appendage. She has the poise of a classical musician but the youthful little sister who wants to experiment.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0fa1cf6f-ff72-41d5-984a-24720547c484">
      <Text>Elizabeth</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="898dfdfc-d4e1-4871-86fe-7adf6f4ab6b9">
      <Text>(tuning her violin)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b484b3d6-160e-4bb7-a951-253630df010a">
      <Text>Jackie, I’ve been thinking about your band. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c8dee3b8-fb08-4b3a-ad01-d65978350bd6">
      <Text>Jackie</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ddbb5fe6-df85-4833-a858-b193e2ebda0f">
      <Text>(distracted)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="90d1b0d0-d704-46b4-84b2-f158d6d25e11">
      <Text>Yeah?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="956bac58-1e67-4e50-bffd-d8e371783054">
      <Text>ELIZABETH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="9077fc95-fdcf-426f-9088-db3d5e414305">
      <Text>(precocious)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7ec0fccc-0e87-40ad-9f7f-ff0e456b58dc">
      <Text>You need a violin. Queen uses orchestral elements all the time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1fba2ee7-b9fc-4f45-b945-d0cae335d595">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="c1c06b48-5e8f-453c-9136-c42b6d7c7086">
      <Text>(surprised)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f90bda1c-2104-4aa2-9945-8006bcd926a8">
      <Text>You mean ... you want to join forces?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ced31d64-2567-457b-9033-57acb761d745">
      <Text>ELIZABETH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="cdb48976-430b-4efc-b093-44f945d80396">
      <Text>(grinning)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ab66b7f2-0726-48d4-9456-1a134802e715">
      <Text>Yes!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="54306a85-3c51-4f73-9d39-1b155988d8d6">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="17f30a23-1856-4d20-96fd-8d9d84c6b58a">
      <Text>I want to rock ‘n roll!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="2d440a74-82ed-4077-b77a-7d743209923b">
      <Text>Elizabeth plays a violin version of “Bohemian Rhapsody” - classical technique applied to rock music. The result is stunning. She’s been practicing for this moment.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7014299d-c63e-411f-ab17-cabe5fdb41fb">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="d9918976-5b3b-496e-8ca5-7cbcb226c026">
      <Text>(awed)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="deb93d01-fb0b-47e3-8fa5-3d189e6efae7">
      <Text>Elizabeth ... that’s ... that’s exactly what we need ... </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5ccb4c59-5aa4-4bd4-96fc-7454a7a67dc1">
      <Text>ELIZABETH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="2a738f40-a8aa-4dc3-b583-7464393f297f">
      <Text>(serious)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d86a7c4c-bf86-4171-be70-a4aae4da6ff4">
      <Text>I don’t want to be decoration. I want to be part of the creative process ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3ea7b224-4124-4d17-8cbc-1eeb976bc7b9">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="b6e53a43-be6f-4272-87d4-3689fcd87b8d">
      <Text>(thinking)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="576b2640-2723-4f47-b0f4-38a265f2fa54">
      <Text>... I can play the piano and the guitar, but we still need a drummer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a293e3a1-9b03-4206-b1e5-2b695814c93f">
      <Text>ELIZABETH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="fec8e58d-68d8-47f9-b1ba-7c49ebdc654f">
      <Text>(playfully)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f6c1cf13-97dc-4de4-9764-745e38a84a8c">
      <Text>Just promise me you won’t wear a leotard.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="51f5f539-14e6-409b-8d81-cdce616f0a2c">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="7800f787-3118-4f9f-aa0d-d1b8648467ce">
      <Text>(laughing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3ffbd346-6d16-4188-a97e-47ba4a95ee90">
      <Text>Deal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="135af5f2-f6da-48bc-a19d-01a29080f570">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 3/8" Page="15" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DAVID CASSEL">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MARK PIANKA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="STEPHEN MURPHY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. Johnson family garage - night</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="c105413f-7ca6-47fe-bc5b-6e444cf3ef39">
      <Text>Nick has assembled his band. Senior STEPHEN “</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">MUP</Text>
      <Text>” MURPHY on bass, a stocky happy-go lucky kid with a good ear. Senior DAVID CASSEL (17) on drums, skinny but powerful with rhythm in his bones. MARK </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">PIANKA</Text>
      <Text> (18) on keyboards, the quite one but musically intuitive. All three band members are from the neighboring and smaller town of Lincoln.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="66164aac-fda4-4468-a091-9f82007024e3">
      <Text>The garage is cramped but electric with energy. The band launches into “Dream On” by Aerosmith. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Note" id="1a8e1966-16bf-4250-b76e-887e3b6699a5">
      <Text>*** Musical Moment</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e5c129b9-c486-4f2d-bd98-8d621014403f">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="52f8097a-dd07-425b-bd3c-e30bd2e95628">
      <Text>(singing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7b4b0510-66bf-4572-ad3c-6dcfd6ac6f2a">
      <Text>Every time that I </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="feda85d7-04ec-479d-9d15-cb364f14b8eb">
      <Text>Look in the mirror</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9114f689-57f4-41ca-b252-ac23622aa736">
      <Text>All these lines on</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2363a967-a80e-4843-b842-6596aeafb688">
      <Text>My faces gettin’</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a5dde2de-e481-4047-9f67-3cb47533bbd3">
      <Text>Clearer</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="da0b552b-b2e4-4565-a29c-2f537d30ff59">
      <Text>The past is gone</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e719aa67-5bb2-496c-b16e-416d366a95fb">
      <Text>It went by like </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="96b6051c-d7c9-412b-b62f-b67a2688ac4c">
      <Text>Dusk to dawn</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="96893550-33f9-4e2c-b67f-716a3a81f88a">
      <Text>Isn’t that the</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c58f15b3-c655-4d86-b86d-1c6727334d63">
      <Text>Way?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5970b4dd-7275-40c8-8192-7ce8861fe292">
      <Text>Everybody’s got</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b249eb84-09b8-4859-b62e-ce18c4940ea5">
      <Text>Their dies in life</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c15f2ffc-b515-4cd0-aa2f-6b250fca7d38">
      <Text>To pay, yeah ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="1ddf1fdf-b700-4ac0-9a97-9e9cb558e01c">
      <Text>As Nick sings he channel’s Stephen Tyler’s distinctive moves - the scarves, the swagger, the way he becomes on with the microphone. The garage walls seem to breathe with the music.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="89d31ab3-cc3a-4aaa-8b22-f0c20c0705fc">
      <Text>STEPhen murphy</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ab129bf8-3b13-4a8e-910f-aad11d506ea6">
      <Text>(bass line driving the song)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0d9c7e82-cbc3-43a2-b5a7-3faae8673b2a">
      <Text>This is it, man. This is what music should feel like.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="254dfb9f-62d3-4064-a82d-1e52d2ca8473">
      <Text>DAVID CASSEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="76959776-3563-4efb-a796-e1c5e23ebeee">
      <Text>Nick, you have Tyler’s moves down, but you’ve got your own voice.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ec58c33a-b764-4c5c-b790-e6c3013c641e">
      <Text>MARK </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">PIANKA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="114abc89-758d-418c-9a19-b4ae3c471308">
      <Text>It’s like Stephen Tyler filtered through Nick Johnson.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="81e030e1-4eb7-4781-8e88-0fbe5b9db5aa">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="fe065fdf-15bf-4201-b061-48974004d273">
      <Text>(continuing and building to the climax)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="326ff503-873d-4437-bad5-0c04202d9bbb">
      <Text>... dream On, dream on</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e2e4a5b0-ab59-48a4-89e0-78395f634f49">
      <Text>Dream on, dream on </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c277754d-0fa2-464d-a782-e6236ed6e09b">
      <Text>Dream until your dreams come true!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="814ebd5d-57f9-46a9-ac98-439646114144">
      <Text>The final note rings out.  The garage holds that perfect musical moment.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2c8c861d-fdd7-401d-89b0-84f433f444ce">
      <Text>STEPHEN MURPHY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="828e29d8-f637-44bf-9a2b-bc36d955c744">
      <Text>(genuinely moved)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7c4c55be-36a7-4518-95bc-521a1f550511">
      <Text>That was fucking beautiful, man.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bfbe6dd2-a400-41ae-a720-a884b8b3dbc7">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f92ccad3-49ab-4a8c-a131-a911f931d0f8">
      <Text>(catching his breath)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5e5987eb-0e64-423f-aae2-e4039dc53c0e">
      <Text>Something took me away ... It’s the song. Aerosmith writes truth for people like us.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a0ab782d-ef82-440e-a1dc-4d4c3887432b">
      <Text>DAVID CASSEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="32bc9be5-d1e0-4d1e-95eb-b242c0bf0876">
      <Text>(innocently)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e31b63ae-84cd-41de-b639-7815cca79fb4">
      <Text>You know what’s crazy? Freshmen year Jackie Marsh used to jam with us Lincoln boys.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="59424ea0-30e1-49af-8f8d-0f1b0dfe537e">
      <Text>STEPHEN MURPHY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="1f5d5b3c-2f5b-485e-b896-43af881ef0c3">
      <Text>(reminiscing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="62c85426-9a9d-47b6-9e23-4be8ece824b4">
      <Text>Remember that first week of freshman year? We were utterly lost souls. Didn’t know anyone from Sudbury, we thought you were all rich kids.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f5e2b918-84bc-412f-8a57-0248e0c92770">
      <Text>DAVID CASSEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0f66fb5b-2090-4f16-aed0-2b38754b29ab">
      <Text>That was Lincoln and Sudbury kids not knowing one another but coming together through music. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="27046dcf-c6e8-4207-910a-5a53be997a8a">
      <Text>STEPHEN MURPHY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9a556ad1-b9ed-4d66-aead-981391737d2c">
      <Text>We did that impromptu mash-up of “Sweet Emotion” and Jackie insisted on “Somebody to Love”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="22df63c6-d4b5-48b2-b59f-23851a46729f">
      <Text>MARK </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">PIANKA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="66e9b5da-fe61-4870-aed4-09bfae6e324a">
      <Text>Heck, it wasn’t great, but it was fun.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="3322f726-d92c-4c59-861f-90998a95b28d">
      <Text>The energy shifts. The musical magic wavers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1c9fa69b-c703-4629-8b4c-dec70ae31549">
      <Text>NiCK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="c1571c26-319d-46ee-bf09-a9cd039e995f">
      <Text>(defensive)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="695ac692-5af6-4b6e-817b-639d1faf07e0">
      <Text>That was right around the same time Jackie decided he was destined for bigger things.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6bdddb7e-5f43-4f3e-acfb-2f6a7d5e875f">
      <Text>DaviD CASSEL</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="514a4eab-c4bb-4b03-aee2-4f52dfc7a76c">
      <Text>(gently)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b2e3ebac-e6de-43e3-ae2c-f7428114b8da">
      <Text>Or when you decided you weren’t read for bigger things?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6869b231-250d-4dcf-8645-f4dd7af7e6f4">
      <Text>Nick</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8f5069b2-3ba7-4e12-a577-8d67078e326b">
      <Text>I had a lot going on ... that was a long time ago.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7c681bdf-5f59-4a94-8037-2899f3ead7c3">
      <Text>STEPHEN MURPHY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d6ad0191-a5c9-4bf0-aec9-6730fa22edb9">
      <Text>You miss him?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3a8b5ed6-484e-41ac-aca5-09f391cd4531">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="bc0c7f3c-f1eb-480c-97eb-39fbb7d255e0">
      <Text>(avoiding the truth)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c2fd33ab-5205-48b3-8175-5763780c94d4">
      <Text>Let’s run through “Back in the Saddle”.  We need to be ... perfect.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="eadb90f7-a91c-46fd-a6c5-357c06456ea4">
      <Text>This new ensemble of teenage boys with hope in their veins launches into the iconic opening riff, but something’s changed. The magic is still there, but it’s tinged with a feeling of loss of innocence from their freshman year. Of what could have been.  </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="ce80f688-9728-4046-90fa-7f09feabbad1">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="17" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. st. Michael’s catholic church - Concord, MA - evening</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="515a14c9-c574-4ca4-87b6-bcf0268d83ab">
      <Text>North of Sudbury in the historical town of Concord, soft acoustic music drifts from stain glass windows. The sound is organic, natural, authentic and poetic in a way that’s different from both Jackie’s precision and Nick’s power.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="a7dbdaeb-a32f-49e1-af9e-371e96d69212">
      <SceneProperties Length="7/8" Page="17" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="PATTY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ROBIN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. St. MICHAEL’s CHURCH - evening</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="d4719bfd-51ac-48dc-aa38-9bcb1e5afcfd">
      <Text>PATTY </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">LALLY</Text>
      <Text> (17) sits at the church piano, her long dirty blond hair catching the light. Patty’s voice is pure magic. A tribute to Stevie Nicks from Fleetwood Mac, but sung with original artistry and tone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a741d604-7b5f-4ade-8e07-efa0bd99a1fe">
      <Text>PAtty</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="af805f1c-4011-4cdb-9c24-12820eb9f116">
      <Text>(singing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d3a34da7-9a4d-4d7f-8ba3-a2ff627057c6">
      <Text>...Don’t stop thinking about tomorrow</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6343acaa-e1a7-4701-a73a-06f29503596c">
      <Text>Don’t stop. It’ll soon be here</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="905cac92-8d2e-4821-8e4c-9d9e473a411e">
      <Text>It’ll be here better than before</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0c6531e1-7788-4126-8cdb-837c4124a5e4">
      <Text>Yesterday’s gone, yesterday’s gone </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="e2544a71-0e92-4f9f-8b03-d5c76fed3756">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aff8e2d5-39f5-4b4e-bb0b-ebc5fb8a7d8c">
      <Text>... Why not think about times to come ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="1c6357fa-955c-4d91-b0b9-5a2b7aced305">
      <Text>Patty’s bandmates harmonize effortlessly. ROBIN BOSSHARD (16) a studious Junior at Concord-Carlisle Regional High understands that thee is something special in the air. Robin digs deeper, closes her eyes and sings from the heart with a softer tone complimenting Patty’s lead.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="95a9787d-fb28-402f-aa6e-c6d4deb91e78">
      <Text>PATTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ba162e70-dbfd-4666-b0c6-ff4622113737">
      <Text>(between songs)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1b66eab0-4a98-4707-b4f5-2b36c822d3c0">
      <Text>Did you hear about the Battle of the Bands at L-S?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9f5a21eb-b948-48a7-9561-df1ab0ae070b">
      <Text>Robin</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="0f19e7d7-5b23-43bc-b64b-2d67e095c1ed">
      <Text>(nervous)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6bfc9692-f08a-413f-a5f4-b6058e3f4ebd">
      <Text>Seems a bit scary. You interested?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="63f303ff-4ea7-4633-96a2-d587c56ff324">
      <Text>PATTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="3722b6e1-21d3-4c0f-af7a-bb7f0a2da18b">
      <Text>(shrugging)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b6acf8dc-3276-4bd1-80e9-77a8f302f7e7">
      <Text>Could be fun. We could use the recording session ... and maybe some </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">WBCN</Text>
      <Text> exposure ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="01b487a3-0d73-4d77-a7f7-f8ebf01f44a7">
      <Text>ROBIN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ee90f303-b815-485c-8a10-0ed97fd7b644">
      <Text>(in all seriousness)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4bedf468-7776-4786-895e-bc4e3e2312c9">
      <Text>I’d have to ask my parents first.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="eab335d4-cc9a-416e-970e-0955025c20a7">
      <Text>They have no idea what lies ahead.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="96fff110-814e-49f8-ba4f-902d038ac28e">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 2/8" Page="18" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MR. WENTWORTH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. LINCOLN-SUDBURY HIGH SCHOOL - MUSIC ROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="75829c70-19f7-4934-b5b3-8d77ef020a4a">
      <Text>The two bulletin boards now show eight bands written in with magic markers. Jackie and Nick stare at the two boards on opposite sides of the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="1647bb45-3b0c-44aa-a51a-87a5ddb623fd">
      <Text>Band names include:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="803edadc-ee44-4361-9644-2d115c94c2a5">
      <Text>1. The Jackson Five tribute band from Boston Latin High School</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="803edadc-ee44-4361-9644-2d115c94c2a5">
      <Text>2. KISS tribute band from </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Acton-Boxboro</Text>
      <Text> Regional High School</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="85797b6e-9a18-4c3e-80b6-be54484b2011">
      <Text>2. ZZ TOP tribute band from Wayland High School</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="2e54e48e-916b-47de-ad8b-60bec3fe20e2">
      <Text>3. Grateful Dead tribute band from Framingham North High School</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="2a56ad99-223b-488a-ae09-a559e6602d3e">
      <Text>4. Marvin Gaye tribute band from Brockton High School</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="04646ac9-c0df-48e0-acd9-fc2270b54528">
      <Text>5. Grateful Dead </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b702966f-8db4-4bed-97ad-ef41eefcad81">
      <Text>6. Aerosmith tribute band from Lincoln-Sudbury High School</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="afdc5009-1be6-40bc-b765-9a2934b5afb7">
      <Text>7. Queen tribute band from Lincoln-Sudbury High School</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="a7b7cdd9-cf79-4d33-937c-b0b8c4335829">
      <Text>8. </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Rumours</Text>
      <Text> a Fleetwood Mac tribute band from Concord-Carlisle</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7fcf8af0-0394-4602-ba04-5a796cd16c9b">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="901004db-9dae-4733-b02d-dd737354d421">
      <Text>(reading)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6435ba2e-480a-4515-99cc-9949c62aafe5">
      <Text>“</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Rumours</Text>
      <Text>”? What kind of name is that?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6112fe3a-ef92-452f-ac22-cea1c0c9bc73">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f59b9b3a-618b-4e9f-b5da-625db116af38">
      <Text>(from across the room)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="045e488a-c79c-4733-b2d0-0ea98235040d">
      <Text>Sounds like Fleetwood Mach </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">wannabees</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="6c0b66bd-223e-4f26-a74f-8aa8b8e75022">
      <Text>For a moment they almost share a look of mutual dismissal like the old days when they dismissed Disco, but then they remember that they are rivals now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c94252c2-2ed9-487c-85e6-3cfc3b89e27f">
      <Text>MR. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f75c8084-1d52-4f7e-8136-3383bc1df751">
      <Text>(entering)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9d60d6e4-c4f5-4463-9a02-19a950e8ca1b">
      <Text>Boys, I need to talk to you both.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="5602807f-ffb1-41d6-b1b1-995414bc245a">
      <Text>They reluctantly move closer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="563d73db-2b2c-4d81-815e-67bc283ee4a3">
      <Text>MR. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6649027b-a621-44ed-ae3d-1378b6e260bb">
      <Text>This competition ... it’s supposed to celebrate a diversity of music, not destroy friendships.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c3f0957e-0935-49cb-a6b4-fa5c39209a04">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="12918347-3445-41b6-bb52-e5fb88e311cb">
      <Text>(defensive)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9ccc46b1-8153-410f-a5ce-64bca2ec473a">
      <Text>We’re fine, Mr. Wentworth.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f4194434-3c95-46d3-afb3-cda39fc136cd">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b37fd916-d602-47da-8e4a-c1a5d27b1dd4">
      <Text>No problems here.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a08f7157-d541-453e-9f11-4b8bb1d1158d">
      <Text>MR. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="e252cea1-86e6-4db1-a9fe-a8c3394a3477">
      <Text>(sighing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="517415b7-a377-408f-b7ae-bb4eeb800a21">
      <Text>Right. Just remember - the best music come from truth, not from trying to prove something.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="e498f263-fbda-473f-9227-c549ae7ac562">
      <SceneProperties Length="1" Page="20" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ELIZABETH">
