          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="STEPHEN MURPHY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Ext. LINCOLN-SUDBURY HIGH SCHOOL - Parking lot - day</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Note" id="02f1f9d2-300e-4317-8caa-078bee14f76a">
      <Text>*** Musical Moment</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="87970bf1-ad8c-459f-ba5e-703c3b042d80">
      <Text>The parking lot has become an unofficial loading dock. Jackie and Nick’s bands both borrowing music equipment for weekend band practice.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="bf992ac6-bcb6-4c1f-828c-c2fe6a42a04e">
      <Text>They work thirty feet apart, pointedly ignoring each other. Jackie turns on his boom box first. Queen’s “Somebody to Love”. Nick counters with Aerosmith’s “Draw the Line”. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="7e7e932a-0f3b-416d-b725-3314a630a771">
      <Text>The parking lock becomes a musical face-off. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="7e7e932a-0f3b-416d-b725-3314a630a771">
      <Text>Band members continue to work, loading musical equipment into a new Ford F-350 (Jackie’s band) and a beat up old Chevy Truck(Nick’s band).  </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="7e7e932a-0f3b-416d-b725-3314a630a771">
      <Text>Both bands work in synchronicity with their music. Band members don’t look up, but they are all singing and their physical movements are in perfect harmony.  </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="630fb759-f978-4ea9-8d7c-3cab60d67de5">
      <Text>EliZABETH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ab7dbe55-e154-4870-84c4-929a9e98c8f0">
      <Text>(approaches Jackie)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4ac2d54a-b528-4df4-b954-8416ac2868f4">
      <Text>This is stupid. You two were inseparable.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="34c3ed13-a31b-4801-87ce-39c64f669e9f">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="5916bd2a-9547-48b2-9530-3b64f722006f">
      <Text>(still singing and working)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f5ecc019-677d-4d46-b223-aaf3926bb563">
      <Text>I miss who he used to be.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="72ba0a84-1494-4a08-8fd3-acc8dddc0ea4">
      <Text>StepHEN MURPHY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ef47b509-d1d3-4442-86b0-d71adb232a74">
      <Text>(to Nick, over the music)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b06b58a4-a044-487a-bac0-00c5864ce275">
      <Text>You’re both being stubborn.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9dcde15d-8bc9-4eda-a723-a3178fd5f896">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="138b1b54-4488-4ece-8da2-444a5a84e841">
      <Text>(still singing and working)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4284f34f-8f03-41b8-ac8b-ea0b60e5b40a">
      <Text>He’s the one who changed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="0e6f26c9-6b73-4c17-ad37-cb32eeea8139">
      <Text>The music fades simultaneously as the trucks are packed. In the sudden silence it seems like either or Jackie or Nick are having second thoughts and might reconsider. Then Mrs. Marsh beeps her horn and and Elizabeth scampers off &amp; Nick’s friends call him away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="28741bb7-97e5-4b72-b9fe-3621f38950a2">
      <Text>The moment passes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="9f7d0442-6f4d-41c6-9c4d-06289b99a34f">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="21" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DR. MARSH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ELIZABETH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. MarSH FAMILY HOUSE - dining room - night</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="25f63eed-901a-4037-9e70-a445cc11828e">
      <Text>The family sits around their formal table. Jackie picks at his food, distracted.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a00a0f33-bc0c-46e3-aef6-492b660e04b5">
      <Text>DR. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="0b03bea6-2488-4239-a8a1-7e99ae22266a">
      <Text>(studying his son)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0cc3d622-9964-4358-8a34-f2200a0a7237">
      <Text>Jackie, you’ve been quiet lately.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7a4a3a3f-2c98-477f-bb61-ea6ef19b202c">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f1680d8d-d70e-4116-b40e-1574e5e6f4de">
      <Text>(looking up)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f5d31c57-78cd-420b-a0af-0ad54fe9a543">
      <Text>Dad, can I ask you something personal?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ff6b3fe1-ab10-4e1f-b143-c971eece0a39">
      <Text>DR. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6b720962-a190-403c-a11d-b439c5599790">
      <Text>Of course.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1cee8a7e-3235-451d-87e9-3661388e5934">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d1751bb3-2880-4aa1-8789-ca06dbc2481f">
      <Text>Did you ever play in a band?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="4b3d5576-9d9a-4129-9ba9-65437df533f0">
      <Text>The question hands in the air. Mrs. Marsh and Elizabeth exchange glances.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1ad4202d-fe61-4ef2-b529-7fd3aa72839b">
      <Text>DR. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="98b28245-7453-44a3-ab55-971bfa106000">
      <Text>(long pause)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4b39429d-4017-45c0-9414-950dccb2cdad">
      <Text>I played guitar in college. Had a band called “The Equations” </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="2a76fbe3-62bf-4e78-a46a-eefe78970c0d">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="76c1d561-3d51-4a5b-802d-b73686564166">
      <Text>... Being a math major and all ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="897abf32-27ce-41f4-87b6-c51aee3ba7d7">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="400b2bec-5391-452e-8696-8a08d2493afe">
      <Text>(</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">suprised</Text>
      <Text>)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d60adae5-4ac1-4a7b-a6c7-4723cad799bf">
      <Text>What happened?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9be56c1c-3f4f-4537-8fa1-57b68d86fd36">
      <Text>DR. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="0700b163-e9be-4de4-a579-c787992dae22">
      <Text>(honestly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6c17bc16-f5aa-4fc1-a24e-308744350e4e">
      <Text>Life happens. Responsibility. Rent, food bills, marriage, family ... I chose between music and security.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="485b3197-243d-4059-8f59-701547bccfee">
      <Text>JackiE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ace63d19-5641-48c4-8507-f4e0488316da">
      <Text>Do you regret it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a708fefc-7caa-4ae1-b405-3ec0aecb901c">
      <Text>Dr. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="da9fd3ab-81bd-4692-be40-3079387c4ade">
      <Text>(suddenly more self-aware)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d3b876e6-217b-4033-b9c7-970331423ce8">
      <Text>I regret ... I regret ... that I see music as an either-or choice. Maybe it doesn’t have to be that way ... </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a8bfd562-a704-4205-a06f-9fd85db9514a">
      <Text>ELIZABETH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="c359b291-d768-4635-9795-c5b244d2cd76">
      <Text>(jumping in)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="770b54e4-a4c4-4018-9213-30f04ec5d36e">
      <Text>Dad, you should hear what Jackie is doing. He’s bringing classical training to rock music.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0facad05-2483-43e0-9da4-15d527bd5d62">
      <Text>Dr. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f9af6a49-9a88-4cc3-ab70-1688d6b7c35d">
      <Text>(interested)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8514a1a1-2706-4fbe-ad7a-c77ad95cb734">
      <Text>Like Freddie Mercury?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bf640feb-32cd-4076-b4a9-f389b1014cf9">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="e64daca6-9bb3-490b-a4e5-21e045b6e0bd">
      <Text>(excited)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="64ab5cde-d35e-42f0-b182-ce0eca03a2b3">
      <Text>Like Freddie Mercury. Using operatic techniques to make rock more more powerful.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7b28524d-240e-4607-925a-9ee76ae3f368">
      <Text>Dr. MARSH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="e921e8d1-e512-45bc-a052-c148f5d52f82">
      <Text>(smiling)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c99b4b16-9ed9-422c-b583-02caa27eef65">
      <Text>Maybe that’s not running away from your training after all ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="b072ad85-5f35-4198-8dc6-3136e4ec4716">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 4/8" Page="22" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MARY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. JohnsoN FAMILY HOUSE - Kitchen - night</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="d400ee9d-e990-4f26-9437-a0bdadf4c860">
      <Text>Nick sits along eating Captain Crunch for dinner. His mother comes home exhausted.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d0545444-4edf-42aa-afc3-2ee33bdf7f30">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="fb7659f4-a168-48c5-b3fb-60afb3f5901c">
      <Text>(collapsing into chair)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ce275266-d495-4bae-82b7-3c6f820c22fd">
      <Text>How’s the band?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7bd5472a-f431-426d-8852-0eef80e9b698">
      <Text>Nick</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6597ab39-2eb9-4a00-bce8-84afde5f6ce5">
      <Text>Really good. We’re channeling Aerosmith but at the same time making it our own.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d52c0947-3aec-46f3-8be0-544b1628d5a0">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="9f4f00f8-e302-4df9-8e25-1e301b297664">
      <Text>(perking up)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d8e58e80-d2f8-44a1-a562-31e879154e55">
      <Text>Tell me about it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="838383e5-4032-4e24-b2f4-f0d649e4e7f7">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="449a11f8-9dfe-40dc-8b7a-eb15786b6f13">
      <Text>(animated)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ebe7c7ee-8bdb-48e6-8228-8c22e3579f20">
      <Text>It’s like Steven Tyler’s energy but filtered through our own experience. Working-class kids who understand how to dream big.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="786e6f92-1808-42a2-b3e6-0e60bd177d25">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="35d028d2-f58a-4c2a-81c8-3d4af823ce4d">
      <Text>(smiling)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="17e66190-d904-4086-9c8e-c00ac93a1716">
      <Text>That sounds wonderful.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="66f5f0c4-08a4-4ec2-a97b-1caf504462af">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="228ef521-7172-468f-a4cc-244a8a33c0d0">
      <Text>(vulnerable)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="87e1751f-d595-48dd-827c-f4f19fdb8589">
      <Text>Mom, what if I’m not good enough</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4a82c573-3270-41cd-9d62-32b4b0137496">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c5e3d7af-5733-4efe-97d1-9ba8e60102b0">
      <Text>Nicolas Edward Johnson, you are exactly good enough.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dab8e631-534c-4407-b9ca-23d163083759">
      <Text>Nick</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="383acff0-e31e-46a3-855f-ac95c9a1c751">
      <Text>(eating away at him)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a40d7d1a-097c-4c7b-8e22-daeec6398e59">
      <Text>You never told me why Dad left. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="af20e715-0686-4a34-8f7b-f0b0f3e0989b">
      <Text>MARy</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d69613ad-415f-4a06-97c0-9cabf0051725">
      <Text>Well, let me set the record straight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="349b142e-2e1e-4fd6-ba37-9b4f8dd7ac01">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="57533c17-eb89-4b5d-83e5-6d14a3424bb1">
      <Text>Your dad didn’t leave because of you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e200e9cf-f977-4507-8436-50655d1a2f8b">
      <Text>NiCK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="032570d6-a327-4c44-834d-6434228ffee8">
      <Text>But I was never good enough in his eyes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="95f71041-8c37-4a30-b87f-5e6b5c893e47">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="42739cdb-4e45-4c5e-84c7-4ea325373d2d">
      <Text>Vietnam did a number on ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="a225a687-ee6f-40ba-b27a-7b3ad29d97cb">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1f131add-3227-4817-af02-4804725bf646">
      <Text>... your did had his own internal battles to deal with.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2d5a49a5-3579-422c-8322-e35f3d1e6e4e">
      <Text>Nick</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f2a29662-93a0-4cd1-9bdb-22d0a61ab9cb">
      <Text>(bring it back to the present)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="38799766-2ef1-41fa-9843-fb2a281699fb">
      <Text>I know about battles ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a3e6e3c3-e1c5-4438-916b-03793368ad03">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="eb816158-3d1f-4a2c-9b76-b8f4efd5d939">
      <Text>Are you trying to be good enough to win a competition, or good enough to be true to your real self?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a7b589b2-a528-46df-b0c3-659001f3bb9b">
      <Text>Nick</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="615b9e3e-01db-4789-b1be-0364091f4cfb">
      <Text>(confused)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4a109406-bd17-4819-bf5a-85e94db36d02">
      <Text>I am not sure I know the difference anymore.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9aa68bdd-c57b-45db-a5e6-8345d0c6866c">
      <Text>MARY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="de96f894-ecd4-4b1d-b685-8ad990dfca16">
      <Text>(gently)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dea6b84c-6ab2-4fdf-99d0-238b04aef9be">
      <Text>Then maybe it’s time to figure that one out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="acaf7bff-9c78-4a97-8893-ac592ca7ee4e">
      <Text>CUT TO:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="0e5805de-d57b-41e0-9393-979065afb91e">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="23" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. MArsh family house - jackie’s bedroom - nighT </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="5da5e4ec-db70-40cf-bfb8-ee868b853904">
      <Text>Jackie sits on his bed, holding the old black and white photograph of him and Nick. Arm in Arm. Smiling. Middle School Talent Show victors. Happy Days. Queen and Aerosmith.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="ed275e47-f1d8-4345-ab16-dbd2f6ea38e2">
      <Text>From downstairs he hears Elizabeth practicing the violin - a beautiful, complex melody.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0caf0ec0-7771-480f-96cf-0dae786dabec">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="923082ba-199c-4126-a4f8-314ae6d3db84">
      <Text>(to the photograph)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c5e15e22-452c-41e5-a61b-5e977041c768">
      <Text>Remember when we thought we could change the world?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="6ec0114d-3375-4ef3-8002-28f23385e534">
      <Text>Jackie picks up his old guitar and begins playing Queen’s “These Are the Days of Our Lives”.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="66e5ae95-dbeb-4c58-9706-063d38ec5a2d">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="5dc20828-98cf-4e9d-91f6-4b0bbdd8e24b">
      <Text>(softly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e194b43a-63c1-498a-b2cb-5cebb977b00b">
      <Text>Sometimes I get a </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">feelin</Text>
      <Text>’</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="78f4dd54-7fed-46fa-9a5e-0e04207667d9">
      <Text>I was back in the old days, long ago</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a8eaf401-6cbd-45a2-af45-51cbff7e1e20">
      <Text>When we were kids, when we were young</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a029ef51-3dac-4f05-adb6-a50b279bfa83">
      <Text>Things seemed so perfect, you know</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3a8c5a67-d527-4342-87ad-f3a82bae508a">
      <Text>These days were endless, we were crazy, we were young</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="15e16c34-2325-4e34-94a3-0934e984f0d6">
      <Text>The was always </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">shinin</Text>
      <Text>’</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b7a5e257-a8a6-42f8-9986-a42117b8827a">
      <Text>We just lived for fun</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="bb60c22b-6dbd-400a-ac12-2fd6929cfe79">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f2d02c08-85f3-4342-9b9d-c445e41a4616">
      <Text>Sometimes it seems like lately</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d0c311cc-1853-40d5-a211-81aea4b2cf61">
      <Text>I just don’t know</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="076fd47d-dd03-4e06-b133-7909870f3c96">
      <Text>The rest of my life’s been just a show ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="1a0418e4-e78b-430c-8634-7bf87a0173bd">
      <Text>This isn’t theatrical. This is Jackie finally allowing himself to grieve what he’s lost. A friendship. A best friend.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="917bcb63-e449-4d2d-9711-dfdf90961c50">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="24" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. JohnSON FAMILY GARAGE - same time</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b5f3bf75-12ed-4af3-ae99-4f26d4d7dda9">
      <Text>Nick sits on the old milk crates, holding the same photograph. He picks up his guitar and starts playing Aerosmith’s “I Don’t Want to Miss a Thing”.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e8cdc24e-b924-44eb-8de0-321af18bbf42">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="85bafa66-d953-4921-a1ec-fbe107432a27">
      <Text>(singing slowly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c80433f1-b91a-492d-8ac2-8292fcfe6077">
      <Text>Don’t wanna close my eyes</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4db3b587-b678-4b06-82ea-c58af280ddb2">
      <Text>I don’t wanna to fall asleep</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f2fa9842-e1d7-4d4d-98bb-94c8470f9932">
      <Text>‘Cause I miss you baby ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="5ed842e6-5c0c-46dc-b08e-1dcd203a459c">
      <Text>The garage doesn’t pulse with rebellious energy. Instead, it becomes almost sacred - Nick’s rough voice creating something beautiful.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cd0bf013-6d33-4e9d-a558-d2a6c7b4ab99">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f8e59c99-1dbe-46b6-8eae-3578615ca2ad">
      <Text>(fading out)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="fd2f8028-31d2-45c1-8eda-08cb816a49f3">
      <Text>... And I don’t wanna miss a thing ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b42d4b36-1e88-44aa-827d-511956482dba">
      <Text>This is working-class defiance. This is Nick being vulnerable, admitting what he has lost.  A friendship. A best friend.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="d2916517-3408-4017-94c4-ab6387530545">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 1/8" Page="25" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="PATTY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Ext. Sudbury, mA - Various location - Night</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="be994742-867d-4e29-8628-5f6a421bb0ee">
      <Text>The camera pulls back to show both boys in their separate spaces, singing songs that express their pain. Their voices drift into the night air, and for a moment, they seem to harmonize across the distance.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Note" id="97d3a590-08c5-46ec-8a78-eb90726c39d4">
      <Text>*** Musical Moment</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c864b409-c95c-4abe-b5e4-1db10281215f">
      <Text>JACKIE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b97e0b02-dbb7-47d2-81ed-662a91efd95c">
      <Text>Sometimes a get a </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">feelin</Text>
      <Text>’ ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e179bdca-1ebf-4843-9f3f-3987ba28900f">
      <Text>NICK (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9502be5b-86ff-4c1e-9cfb-3f7f9a15c1de">
      <Text>Don’t want to close my eyes ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="acbefd55-aa0f-4ea9-9e2f-0b8653df87fd">
      <Text>JACKIE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="43547dd4-a5d1-48e8-97f5-05115b5100b3">
      <Text>I was back in the old days, long ago ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fae88349-c3f4-4d4d-9145-e93201113c20">
      <Text>NICK (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b14d5140-5263-4c1f-91fe-c6be692c2212">
      <Text>I don’t wanna miss ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="4e90a64f-dbab-4f39-9e7d-512de300b527">
      <Text>The two songs shouldn’t work together, but they do - creating a complex harmony that suggests what could be possible.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="ce55f937-8ef4-4c8b-a0b1-783255480c81">
      <Text>And from the St. Michael’s Church in Concord, Patty’s voice joins the night’s air. Patty belts out Fleetwood Mac’s “Landslide”.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="df21aa47-a9f1-4fcc-9e65-16d860bc6f2e">
      <Text>PATTY (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8f931716-9fbd-4a8f-9d96-9cf8d6e8ba6b">
      <Text>I took my love, I took it down</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="39ac7b98-5798-448b-b880-19095367c6a1">
      <Text>Climbed a mountain and I turned around</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="3222b875-a023-41fb-a09b-dd2e7cbe6369">
      <Text>And I saw my reflection in the snow covered hills</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="794327be-fb78-49ad-bce9-e55761c97aa6">
      <Text>‘Tis the landslide that brought me down ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="f6fffa8f-6248-4788-b17e-41973230bb32">
      <Text>Three voices blend, creating something none could achieve along.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e43c1e6c-88a2-4dbe-abba-3cc81c705052">
      <Text>PaTTY (V.O. CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bfc28d72-8306-425b-ae57-870e382fdc15">
      <Text>... Well I’ve been a ‘</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">fraid</Text>
      <Text> of </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">changin</Text>
      <Text>’</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3475c831-6872-430b-9fbf-9cf47ae6c30a">
      <Text>‘Cause I’ve built my life around you</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="06b7b2aa-c6f0-4f80-a043-1a2d6c9bb9a8">
      <Text>But the time makes you bolder</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="804fde96-da27-4591-98df-00be6f9534e1">
      <Text>Even children get older</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6c49d02e-a2e8-46d0-af31-c13241a486b0">
      <Text>And I’m getting older too ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b5f4549a-65ff-4c58-8e00-cbae3c471b79">
      <Text>But that realization is still weeks away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="bb2eec30-e09d-46cf-97ae-b864cf1c52ff">
      <Text>FADE TO BLACK.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="New Act" id="1ac1b663-4aed-4749-88cb-94e1773273b0">
      <Text>ACT II.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="417819ff-c27e-410e-b10d-2f14a8154096">
      <SceneProperties Length="7/8" Page="27" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BAND">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="STEPHEN MURPHY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. JoHNSON FAMILY garage - night</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Note" id="f299de81-46e3-4d95-b2c7-669c2f0b6b2c">
      <Text>*** Musical Moment</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="a3db44b0-b5f3-47ba-9577-cfdadf416464">
      <Text>Nick’s Aerosmith practicing. The band launch into “Dream On”.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7f8696a3-2fa8-42e7-8b6a-eea6a8574b7c">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="1831e3c1-b7b4-4038-b1a6-c0bc81bf4f71">
      <Text>(fire in the belly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bb725d2a-28bd-487f-81be-41fe36598df9">
      <Text>Every time that I look in the mirror</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="50098996-c532-47cb-ad1a-cf2a88bdd035">
      <Text>All these lines and my face getting clearer</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="82da4c9f-c88d-4a33-a20a-7e06eaf7156e">
      <Text>The past is gone</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="76051b2f-ed9e-4291-967e-a0af7dbb71e9">
      <Text>Oh, it went by dusk to dawn</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6276fcc7-cd50-4999-9fe7-39a4db7ecf8c">
      <Text>Isn’t that the way?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="925e2763-cf70-4ea9-9eb5-472c4af0de77">
      <Text>As Nick sings, the garage walls breathe with the music. This isn’t controlled perfection of Jackie’s room - this is raw, authentic, emotion manifested.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8c23e21e-524a-4372-8690-580c6d83b9c9">
      <Text>BAND</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="738d4ab9-ee54-4d5e-9fe8-97b1ca3a8e8e">
      <Text>(singing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2372071a-0fbd-464f-95e7-674b9ec8d060">
      <Text>Dream on</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d75cf7b3-7be1-492f-bc8c-81006013c385">
      <Text>Dream on</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7c2582ac-a3c6-4a0b-8b28-5129303c2c67">
      <Text>Dream on</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a77eab04-19f2-494d-933c-e577f67e6928">
      <Text>I’ll dream on</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="95cc366e-8f6e-4acf-ab6d-f87e60a1a0a5">
      <Text>Dream on</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="93a27c41-f66b-49ab-b031-a292a52c4fb2">
      <Text>Dream on </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6065c5f9-3ea1-4a29-b6ab-4e801806fc71">
      <Text>I dream on ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="ed730245-0992-456c-85ee-68e97f70e0ff">
      <Text>The final note rings out, and for a moment, the garage holds that perfect musical moment. These are no ling kids playing dress-up - they’re creating something real.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="475c97ea-bba8-4113-b02e-a36ebb450566">
      <Text>StEPHEN MURPHY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="baa9b45a-c6a5-40a2-b930-0e212efff18d">
      <Text>(grinning, genuinely moved)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0b5ce520-00c1-44e0-b28c-68a341137293">
      <Text>Yeah! That was fucking beautiful!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="63c22954-727a-4fa2-965b-23e622ce4faa">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="85cb39a1-071f-4a3a-bf2e-4a570293ee92">
      <Text>(modest)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="898db1b1-5faa-4737-92f4-c9c7264a25b1">
      <Text>Aerosmith writes the truth.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="4c91aff8-4e9b-4fea-8a07-6157353ffd3d">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="27" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. MARSH FAMILY HOUSE - Basement - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="60345e75-0767-4586-90f5-18556a636ea2">
      <Text>The family basement has been converted into a music studio suitable for recording. Queen’s collection of Albums neatly displayed on the walls.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="da912c33-a1c8-40f9-9d49-92315afd4c90">
      <Text>ARTHUR “ACE” CALLAHAN (14) has joined the band. He has steady hands and plays the drums with utmost precision.  Ace is in Elizabeth’s freshman class, but even at this tender age he is poised and confident. The first freshman to start on the L-S Varsity Soccer Team.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b4682fa7-d90b-4cf3-81d9-80dae2d35c0b">
      <Text>MAX WESSLEN (15) hasn’t quite grown into his body. He’s lean and tall. He’s methodical on the bass. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="7e491f2a-3f62-4c44-9238-7c9ae5645c84">
      <Text>Jackie is the jack of all trades and seemingly growing into the persona of Freddie Mercury. He bounces between the piano, vocals and the guitar. A jack of all trades. Elizabeth rounds the band out and keeps things honest with her violin and backup vocals.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="f59e5f21-1ddc-4b4c-a846-27a0871622ad">
      <Text>Ace signals ... one-two-three ... tapping his drumstick on the rims of his Yamaha YD-9000 drum set.  The band launches into Queen’s “Don’t Stop Me Now”. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="a6af61fc-9751-4406-8c24-e189f289fbf7">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="28" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. LINCOLN-SUDBURY HIGH SCHOOL, Morning (two weeks later)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="d8544e19-03ba-486d-ae4d-d6f3abb1d2ae">
      <Text>The school buzzes with “Battle of the Bands” fever as if this were the State Basketball Championships.  This isn’t just the musicians, this is the gym teachers, science teachers, math teachers, administrators, “</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RAMPERS</Text>
      <Text>”, “RATS” and “REGS” alike.  </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="05c154a2-56d5-475c-a361-4fff7fe1374a">
      <Text>Homemade posters cover the walls celebrating the Band of choice. The divide isn’t just between Jackie and Nick anymore - it’s infected the whole school.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="0e1cf35f-8c61-4c04-825d-47d197b1bf88">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="28" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RAMPER QUEEN FAN #2">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RAT AEROSMITH FAN #2">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="REG AEROSMITH FAN #1">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="REG QUEEN FAN #1">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. LINCOLN-SUDBURY HIGH - GLASS CORRIDOR - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b723e461-7767-42e8-8bb2-12e4fe7cd227">
      <Text>The </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RAMPERS</Text>
      <Text> and REGS dart through the Glass Corridor pushing away the cigarette smoke.  </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0dba8d1f-9940-459c-8597-0ce5aed3f47e">
      <Text>REG Queen fan #1</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="04451590-3fd2-4de5-9df9-b4a1fcaff1b0">
      <Text>(Queen concert T-shirt)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8f05c94d-6e90-4b89-bd8c-58ff55087672">
      <Text>Queen is going to demolish everyone. I heard Jackie has a personal voice coach ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0d9ae86f-12c0-4ffa-a788-87c534abffe6">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RAMPER</Text>
      <Text> QUEEN FAN #2</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="19a95b3f-b5aa-419a-b03a-075b2b85e8f5">
      <Text>... early admission to Cornell, but he hasn’t accepted it ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e49ab20a-3689-4112-a688-374be33bb6ec">
      <Text>REG AeroSMITH FAN #1</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="1140ba67-7e14-4e4b-ac52-d54b3cdd2239">
      <Text>(faded Aerosmith concert T-shirt)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e0ff0a2d-4bc1-4320-8cb1-135e23a1224f">
      <Text>Aerosmith has soul, true rock and roll.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="75546012-7b1d-41e7-b165-3284788c293b">
      <Text>RAT Aerosmith FAN #2</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="3967787e-00ae-4c25-8647-b0cbff6f1b16">
      <Text>(joining in)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="083a5976-0ce7-4283-8d99-c7defc5c71d0">
      <Text>Nothing beats Aerosmith ... did you know they are from Boston?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="0b931d6f-e332-413d-b62a-2c56ea258b6a">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 2/8" Page="29" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="CROWD-OF-WOULD-BE-ROCKSTARS">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MICK JAGGER WANNABE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MR. WENTWORTH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="STEVIE WONDER WANNABE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="STUDENT COORDINATOR">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. LINCOLN-SUDBURY HIGH - MUSIC ROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="5da7c354-f6b5-4bdb-a302-14d055f2f289">
      <Text>Mr. Wentworth stares out at the chaos he’s unleashed. He’s turning away new groups that went to enter the Battle of the Bands. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="61abafd5-45c4-4ee0-8c4d-a213092a17a4">
      <Text>Students line up to practice, band schedules cover his desk and tension is palpable.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d68987a4-8fce-4ea0-a873-872165d1340a">
      <Text>Student coordinator</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6f0d31fb-ecb0-4c2c-9af6-912adcfd506f">
      <Text>Mr. Wentworth, we need to talk about practice time. Queen wants the good acoustics room, but Aerosmith was here first,</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="8dbe636e-03f2-47f4-8d1a-5f9b69086004">
      <Text>The leader of a seemingly new formed group ROLLING STONES is hot under the collar as he’s in a heated discussion with Mr. Wentworth while six other newly formed cover bands hover around. Most of them have not graduated from 3rd grade Choir.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="950eca4b-9ce8-4ad0-b970-dcd06a3b951f">
      <Text>MICK JAGGER Wannabe</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="8b841979-62c9-485d-9259-cbfd89c9f45b">
      <Text>(english accent, angry)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a7d78f83-b695-4514-87db-a4dd39d13254">
      <Text>... that’s bloody bullocks!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5ef08c90-7603-4728-9a35-e6e2ef2f0819">
      <Text>MR. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5b014f66-7896-4a5d-9979-a6c71cb4ff95">
      <Text>It’s a district contest, I can’t change things now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="6223d753-a90d-473b-b9d4-8ce02388e1b3">
      <Text>Mr. </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Wentwork</Text>
      <Text> takes another glance at the musical melting pot that’s brewing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4849ca30-da7b-45bc-ac98-6d2f719e3434">
      <Text>MICK JAGGER WANNABE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a45c80b8-2f76-40eb-9682-68d94a7f3106">
      <Text>Bloody well right you can.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8168bfa9-d0ba-4d7d-b90a-387e061df20c">
      <Text>Stevie wonder wannabe</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="cf89ff01-46c8-45c0-aff3-cc9432b550ae">
      <Text>(singing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ce655559-a079-4c73-9b86-305eebfc3843">
      <Text>Very superstitious, nothing more to say</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="00b6159a-9f0d-4c1e-91c4-32e1ae6659e9">
      <Text>Very superstitious the devil’s on the way</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a2c2002e-f7a8-41da-9dd2-f0aa3c515179">
      <Text>Superstition ain’t the way, yeah, yeah ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="7f8a3b51-7457-4d18-9b7d-1c3197d542e7">
      <Text>(changes persona)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="06957927-8eae-4e67-9d44-bc572edd9815">
      <Text>Let’s take this up Principal Sargent ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2d962d9a-d0c7-470c-a5f9-1ae4326e1b43">
      <Text>CROWD-OF-would-be-rockstars</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="1873ae6c-f339-4154-b4a0-b88cee71b190">
      <Text>(chanting)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7c42614b-0f56-495e-beaa-d36c8daca4e8">
      <Text>Sergeant, Sergeant, Sergeant ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c9768f68-0cd0-43cf-8635-b375e0c39979">
      <Text>Mr. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1402574e-16b7-43be-8438-b52995f0e008">
      <Text>Next year, next year ... keep up the practicing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="ac241f2c-8f92-4828-89f8-271072578613">
      <Text>Within the crowd a JOHN LENNON LOOK-A-LIKE is suddenly inspired to start singing “Sgt. Pepper/s Lonely Hearts Club Band”. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="ac241f2c-8f92-4828-89f8-271072578613">
      <Text>Kids plug their ears. His voice is like glass in a garbage disposal. The music crowd disperses. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5619abf5-5fba-4a11-8425-db20f4391eb5">
      <Text>MR. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="edd60f4c-a995-4618-a6c4-e6746b8c0a8a">
      <Text>(tugging at his bow tie)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="76dd4004-8e2e-4c1a-a7b2-8171ab05d965">
      <Text>This was supposed to be about music exploration, not tribal warfare.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="20517842-1ed2-47a6-83f2-dd9e4a55dece">
      <SceneProperties Length="1" Page="30" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MARK PIANKA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="STEPHEN MURPHY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. johnson FAMILY GARAGE - Day</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="26baf8ec-9744-493f-bb17-344d78c19fc6">
      <Text>The garage pulses with raw energy. Aerosmith practice with passionate intensity. The look they are having a lot of fun. Nick’s expression indicates that he is loosening up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ea121265-c537-4f75-99f0-8ff72ed26306">
      <Text>StePHEN MURPHY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="58978d39-72a3-44bf-b5da-0452ad4d451f">
      <Text>(pause between songs)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bbf3479c-4c13-4dc7-9745-761cc1895fcf">
      <Text>Music isn’t about being perfect. It’s about being real.  I heard that somewhere but can’t remember where.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e41887ba-2776-46bb-b081-72e1b0d10551">
      <Text>MARK </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">PIANKA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="b346b23b-7d3e-4762-99bd-083aaa95be21">
      <Text>(adjusting his keyboard)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c32e22da-c35a-417a-9151-1c80cff316c8">
      <Text>That’s why people connect with Aerosmith. They aren’t trying to be Gods. They’re trying to be human.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3468cc59-4b0f-4c19-8871-0e6cf485f11e">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="b4231220-8784-41a9-97a2-9b4aaafda118">
      <Text>(tuning his guitar)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="70595b14-a422-4dae-84a5-a4715497ee1c">
      <Text>Jackie doesn’t understand that anymore. He thinks music is about being perfect.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="aba5c44d-3bf9-4762-8011-83c24abf2d95">
      <Text>STEPHEN MURPHY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="36a9244a-d498-443b-a7ee-a80be29309d1">
      <Text>(half joking)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9b946e95-b07b-4f65-98c4-1d1b075f8be6">
      <Text>But Aerosmith is still God-like!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="19bfba1e-e46a-4629-bf81-a22bbfd559ec">
      <Text>They band launches into “Sweet Emotion” and the garage becomes electric. The walls seem to breathe with the music, tools vibrate in harmony and the concrete floor pulses with authentic rhythm. The garage is authentic and real. Concrete and wood.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1503898f-c0c2-461d-8eac-30e28d12dcaf">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ac594086-cccd-44d9-8e86-51527dcec8cc">
      <Text>(singing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aae2bfd5-21b4-4719-9d7f-59efefd69b86">
      <Text>Sweet Emotion</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="de4e797e-4d65-444a-8e6a-cb76e6971879">
      <Text>Sweet Emotion</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f439971f-3dd3-4712-9a85-e8120e643e3c">
      <Text>You talk about things that nobody cares</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="48d61103-5e42-466b-a61a-fc457f036a50">
      <Text>You’re wearing out things that nobody wears</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="510e7020-2cbf-42bf-86b4-39d387250794">
      <Text>You’re calling my name but I gotta make clear</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bdb60576-2534-4d32-be33-624cc9cfb8c5">
      <Text>I can’t say baby where I’ll be in a year ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="20517842-1ed2-47a6-83f2-dd9e4a55dece">
      <SceneProperties Length="7/8" Page="31" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ACE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MAX">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. MARSH FAMILY HOUSE - BASEMEnt - same time</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="29f81ecd-1289-4c98-8ac4-1cbd75e7be89">
      <Text>Ace is spinning his drumsticks and ready to rock. Max cradles his bass.  </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0bd10519-adf6-46ab-a1bc-710025703013">
      <Text>ACE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="5292bd01-4e83-4957-9850-e355031dce6e">
      <Text>(continues to spin his drumsticks)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3f1f19ff-fc8f-4aa7-a9b7-9b016bfc3d25">
      <Text>Queen is precise about tempo and we need to work on this.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="30ecfbfe-2f20-4c4b-95d4-db3fc09270a6">
      <Text>MAX</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="40488070-fc2f-4cac-b18b-6577a839e43c">
      <Text>(quietly questioning)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9797276e-b055-423e-87e5-756163b329f9">
      <Text>But what if we made it our own? Added something personal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1a5aa10f-a298-4c52-935a-2024a0b3ec90">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="793d19ae-a9ae-4022-8e1c-1b686195a8fd">
      <Text>(commanding)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0223f85b-2d39-4de0-98f6-48ce1847a31a">
      <Text>Ace is right. We’re not here to reinvent Queen. We’re here to honor them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="31190476-be6e-4bef-8452-e3dc523b8b42">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c4150075-3392-4d17-9fba-562383041eb5">
      <Text>From the top ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="a94669c2-1936-441b-a85c-a19df4cc7f54">
      <Text>The band launches into “We will Rock You” with technical brilliance, but something feels rehearsed, manufactured. The basement transforms into a concert hall, but it’s cold, impressive rather than moving.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="99afb7aa-31e0-4a14-a39b-1daa71ccb6aa">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="b78fe408-a3b9-4b1c-90bf-ea0ecd7e2f75">
      <Text>(singing with perfect technique)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d3906227-03f4-41b8-9cdf-21173148424e">
      <Text>Buddy, you’re a boy, make a big noise</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3bc1e886-b69d-4fc2-bd21-9120973ccfc2">
      <Text>Playing in the street, gonna be a big man someday</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fb5af180-b0da-4412-af5a-54fb2c8e0d5e">
      <Text>You got mud on your face, you big disgrace</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="34b4fa8b-a725-4563-aff2-9a96ee32c17a">
      <Text>Kicking you can all over the place, </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">singin</Text>
      <Text>’</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6ea526e7-82da-47f4-8ca2-7def40570d0c">
      <Text>We will, we will rock you</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="32c6988d-c068-4048-99af-e4d24f166d11">
      <Text>We will, we will rock you ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b27cd157-2dcb-48bb-86f9-f2f767953d0b">
      <Text>The harmonies are now flawless, but Max looks uncomfortable wit the rigid approach.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="8f55dc2d-61c6-4c5d-bd9e-f2ccc32626a1">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="32" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MAXANNE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">WBCN</Text>
      <Text> radio STATION - 171 newbury st. - Back BAy - DAY </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="f6a74dc4-2924-4edb-a07d-c45f0791d2fa">
      <Text>MAXANNE SATORI sits behind the microphone.  Working-class DJ running the studio speakers at full volume.   </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d9a54d97-4a01-49df-9a22-a2f88984fb9f">
      <Text>MAXANNE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8132d990-e09f-42fd-810a-5906b94f5998">
      <Text>... that was the Eagles with “Life in the Fast Lane and before that Aerosmith with “Train Kept A-Rollin” ... </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="1fdc752b-8bfc-4107-9b9c-b9477e4c627b">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="069059a3-ac4b-44e7-aeb6-0218da616afc">
      <Text>... a quick shutout to Lincoln-Sudbury High’s “Battle of the Bands” on March 15th... </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="cf2c570c-317e-4c12-9e8c-8fdd7085fc4c">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4ed7fd47-8db7-4d67-b8b1-36ac3dbe1684">
      <Text>Next up is good friend, Bruce Springsteen and his unplugged performance of “</Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Rosalita</Text>
      <Text>” heard here on radio Ten-Four in Boston, </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">WBCN</Text>
      <Text> ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="44167b39-3bf3-4caa-9859-51722bf15766">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="32" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Ext. Sudbury town center - day</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="c8920ce9-a803-4dd9-a8aa-2d2f540585f9">
      <Text>The Battle of the Bands has become a community event. Local businesses now display “Queen” and “Aerosmith” signs. The hardware store supports Nick’s working-class appeal, the bookstore back Jackie’s sophistication.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="d9b35210-094d-4fb8-b157-a71166643431">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="32" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="FRANK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. TOWN LINE HARDWARE - SUDBURY - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="73f13cdb-8ea9-4c07-b022-ae4e41ffe5e1">
      <Text>FRANK </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">TASKOVICS</Text>
      <Text> (50s), the store owner, puts up an “AEROSMITH” poster in the window.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="05eb1946-850b-4c8b-a422-4913d78bb946">
      <Text>FRANK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ed60769f-1ca1-4c4d-b4fe-83e8ca786a03">
      <Text>(to an employee)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2afafe7f-ad4b-4f50-a32c-6d7a165dbf4e">
      <Text>These kids understand what it’s like to work for a living. Nick Johnson’s father used to come in here every Saturday morning. We served together in ‘Nam ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="c9fc4e82-521b-4400-b5e3-e58d9f19531b">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="33" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KRISTIN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. bentley’s bookstore - sudbury - day</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="c22bc0a5-13ef-49d0-b5e5-f1c0dbe99ac2">
      <Text>KRISTIN </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">WADMAN</Text>
      <Text> (45), the bookstore owner, displays a “QUEEN” poster and lined up the original Queen’s books for sale hoping to cash in on Battle of the Bands hype. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d3c88374-f4e0-467d-ac51-fc9b5ce69283">
      <Text>KristIn</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ad2d73d6-6e7f-49c5-b853-154a8f84655c">
      <Text>(to a customer)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="57d87c67-4385-4d8a-b2b7-84fa804fd4c5">
      <Text>That Jackie Marsh represent the best of Sudbury and our community. Destined for great things. His father has some fancy job at B.U.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="0c5024e2-3d88-46ee-9ae3-0a502e3e824e">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 6/8" Page="33" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="COLLEGE-BOUND STUDENT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JACKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MR. WENTWORTH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NICK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="PREPPY UNDERCLASSMAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="WORKING-CLASS STUDENT #1">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="WORKING-CLASS STUDENT #2">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="WORKING-CLASS STUDENT #3">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>Int. LINCOLN-SUDBURY HIGH SCHOOL - CAFETERIA - Day</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="f370b351-e92d-4b49-939d-4a4d34ca093c">
      <Text>The cafeteria has become a war zone. Students sit with their musical allegiances. Jackie and Nick’s table are now surrounded by supporters, creating rival camps.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6e084c57-8c17-4a7f-af64-bae79f198e2b">
      <Text>College-bound student</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="e360254f-eb79-4592-af7a-6c336d0bb652">
      <Text>(at Jackie’s table)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="583022e5-bbb7-420a-ac58-14f9fd1d640c">
      <Text>I heard Jackie is going to do a Queen medley ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dc5d1839-e416-4355-8d4a-7b52163524d2">
      <Text>Preppy underclassman</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6c72a1e8-6147-48f4-ac27-513ae1de62e7">
      <Text>Jackie’s vocal range is insane. He can hit notes that make professional singers jealous ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="00c0266f-bed6-4046-b1e7-814127792125">
      <Text>At Nick’s table, twenty feet away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c9e9b19e-e7d9-4c4d-a02d-89056358be69">
      <Text>Working-class student #1</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5ccd33eb-e66f-43bd-9f59-7aade3f684b8">
      <Text>Aerosmith warmed up at the youth center last weekend. I swear I saw a few tears during “Dream On”.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b3563c16-ca15-4762-8429-2db243bdf884">
      <Text>WORKING-CLASS STUDENT #2</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="17ed3d7c-7a8d-4b93-9b25-95c27ed4bcb7">
      <Text>(Boston accent)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c8c1915c-5545-4838-ad81-a7180c2a0ba6">
      <Text>Yeah, Aerosmith is wicked good. I heard the real band members might attend the Battle of the Bands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8273ccbe-7c1c-4b73-a549-f1108229e9e9">
      <Text>WORKING-CLASS STUDENT #3</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="be03ee38-3d35-46fe-9991-df644a2d5cc9">
      <Text>Rumor has it that the real band members will attend the Battle of the Bands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7d21e50c-e169-4137-9f08-17d979aa6d82">
      <Text>Working-CLASS STUDENT #1</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6727dce8-5b4a-4315-9f65-09b7766f85ae">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Pissah</Text>
      <Text>!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bcd0947b-d0f9-4a60-97a9-84aa68088ecc">
      <Text>WORKING-CLASS STUDENT #2</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4c05e26e-8108-40d4-8129-69358410c5d1">
      <Text>Aerosmith is not just playing music they’re channeling something real life.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="dcfeb539-089f-4a78-a5e0-77a0350c784d">
      <Text>Jackie overhears and can’t help himself.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="97667028-250f-40c6-baa2-5696e07c91e3">
      <Text>Jackie</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="575b6c80-c8b2-4afe-85ed-5b036520a8dc">
      <Text>(not so quiet)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bf79b8b7-3b91-4796-af53-12df81e8da2d">
      <Text>Real music requires training and discipline. Not just ... feeling.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b27a6146-7be3-40c1-a6b3-c3ebf562c44e">
      <Text>The cafeteria suddenly fall silent. Nick stands up slowly.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c1db021e-4bbc-46dc-a034-0718f12032aa">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="0091cf61-fa55-44fa-a7e9-ceed408b00ca">
      <Text>(countering)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1993b036-f7b2-4bfa-96cf-035b0fb89102">
      <Text>And trained music requires a real soul. Not just ... technique.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="757471f8-b107-48e5-8ee3-3708da80a2d4">
      <Text>The tension is explosive. Students look back and forth between the two former friends like they are watching Bjorn Borg and Jimmy Connors in the Wimbledon final. Two very contrasting styles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7b80bef4-8810-4144-8562-5cbc2b7a426f">
      <Text>MR. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="45ea3356-92d6-476e-b1a0-87f9994e8f6a">
      <Text>(entering the cafeteria)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bd4b4d0d-0c1c-4096-835a-df0f3589995b">
      <Text>Gentlemen, perhaps we should -</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0c1034b5-2fb9-45eb-a3ca-9672e0c76740">
      <Text>Jackie</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="d7c905df-a7a7-4085-8e16-54062e710f11">
      <Text>(interrupting, standing)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="32ffcb5d-4792-461a-bb56-1d2cfec76128">
      <Text>You know what, Nick? Let’s settle this right now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ec4734c5-0254-44f8-8e8e-f54af0e93ec8">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="4120a353-ac5a-4196-b9c2-0899b7a120d2">
      <Text>(grinning dangerously)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e8066507-0ca0-4d62-bdf3-f62a00a0cab2">
      <Text>I was hoping you would say that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Note" id="1d115339-138b-4b49-b5a0-1a6ed840dc43">
      <Text>*** Musical Moment</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="92af47c9-dc46-41b4-bb97-3ff495815268">
      <Text>Jackie nods to his band members, who produce instruments from underneath the cafeteria tables. Acoustic guitars, a small Casio VL-1 musical keyboard is plugged in, Ace spins his drumsticks and Elizabeth reveals her violin. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4807609a-c9c2-42c6-b119-3ffdc7c20b57">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="a4783967-c3ca-4a3b-b301-e51cf6599cdb">
      <Text>(to the cafeteria at large)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6cb96955-aed2-49f9-8430-9d05c9e335b5">
      <Text>We Are The Champions ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="aa110b6f-8c0f-4ae7-9d2e-e8b96d28e2ce">
      <Text>Queen launches into their anthem.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="e9598090-1142-4995-a3a6-6ee962e5445d">
      <Text>Jackie’s voice soars through the cafeteria, technically perfect and undeniably impressive. Jackie’s followers begin clapping in rhythm. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f7f0f3b4-524a-4e76-b40b-e8f739eed4df">
      <Text>JACKIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ff9b307e-4b01-41a2-a670-8057ba859687">
      <Text>(singing with precision)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d5be6bb3-2f9d-4e2b-931b-634a98929bf0">
      <Text>... We are the champions, my friends ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b7fe61e9-5140-44ac-b60a-534c324e5693">
      <Text>The cafeteria transform - lunch tables become concert seating, fluorescent light become stage lights and Jackie commands the space like a born performer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="b8c77a42-e68f-4dd4-9385-7b69aad9b637">
      <Text>But when the song ends and he cafeteria transforms back, Nick stands up. The cafeteria transforms into a large working-class garage. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4aa4840e-7e31-4bd3-be6d-64c323f2dd3c">
      <Text>Nick</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="b65214ec-684e-4374-8d67-d96a774fe17d">
      <Text>(to the cafeteria)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d09b376e-8ad1-44f8-970e-9343deaf7575">
      <Text>“Dream On”.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="46752080-ddb4-4512-9a8b-11d24e577c28">
      <Text>Nick steps forward, and without any instruments, begins to sing A </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">capella</Text>
      <Text>. His voice is rougher than Jackie’s, but it carries something deeper - pain, hope, authentic human experience. </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="67386ff0-c442-4dd0-89ea-7482e939d5a3">
      <Text>Nick</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="af27ea5b-a6e5-4fe9-91a8-3dac547de891">
      <Text>... Everybody’s got their dues in life to pay, oh, oh, oh</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="77b0ba0b-0c31-4ae6-8100-6959696be46f">
      <Text>I nobody knows</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="760b1c5a-aa85-4e6c-bcdc-94a948d1f007">
      <Text>Where it comes from and where it goes</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="89b7338c-f43f-42ce-a455-bd96ce6465bf">
      <Text>I know everybody’s sin</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d4a42154-6093-45ad-bae2-4a2b96cd860a">
      <Text>You got to lose to know how to win ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="766052aa-bc0e-49e0-ac28-8a84a1f30df3">
      <Text>The cafeteria is in dead silence.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="486fe2d7-ee6b-425c-a308-f67f5047f1f1">
      <Text>NICK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="4dab56d1-27b2-4dde-bd20-ae1cd08e3210">
      <Text>(eloquently)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="212d8cba-895a-4b86-ae0a-4b48ae469eaf">
      <Text>Dream on</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8cc699de-6b8b-4524-8902-b037b86210b3">
      <Text>Dream on</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cdef9e1d-ea5f-466f-a579-a64b3f66a11a">
      <Text>I dream on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="4fa8af25-6048-4561-a613-b8f8a5d7a765">
      <Text>The final note hangs in the air. The cafeteria remains silent. Both performances are brilliant, but in a completely different ways.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bf9787e7-4bd2-49c4-8f8c-0a7b71d4cd24">
      <Text>MR. WENTWORTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="4b03aec0-3db1-496b-b818-d969eda58b6c">
      <Text>(breaking the silence)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f76020fb-c0c3-4e4e-9dfe-84ad1d5fd8a6">
      <Text>You two should save something for Battle of the Bands ... now come with me ...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="7e5d3a24-a78d-48a4-b2b0-748612638bd5">
      <Text>Jackie and Nick can’t look at each other as they exit with Mr. Wentworth. Finally the cafeteria goes bonkers with loud applause.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
